Okay. Craig, could I— so as clarity, uh, when you say staffing

38:26.000 --> 38:28.920
levels specific to the police department per 1,000, like what's the,

38:29.420 --> 38:32.440
what's the metrics you're looking for? Well, we'll have their population. We can get their

38:32.940 --> 38:36.560
population data. So that's what you want them to get, the staffing

38:37.060 --> 38:40.340
level per population? Are you talking per call volume? Like what's the— I'm more

38:40.840 --> 38:43.860
staffing per population. So we just need to know the total number? That's my main,

38:44.360 --> 38:48.107
that's my main. Okay, good. Okay, perfect. Probably the

38:48.607 --> 38:51.399
only thing I would add, I think it's been a good discussion, is I'm concerned

38:51.899 --> 38:55.557
about fleet services and where that shows up because that will segment into parks,

38:55.573 --> 38:59.250
streets, trails, and open space. I mean, there's a

38:59.750 --> 39:02.782
fleet that we're maintaining and we're employing someone to take care of it, or we're

39:03.282 --> 39:06.700
