02:03:37.055 --> 02:03:41.067
Every city council should be dragged from their seats and

02:03:41.083 --> 02:03:44.372
hanged in the public square, then hang their families for

02:03:44.872 --> 02:03:48.368
their treasonous asses. F them all. You know

02:03:48.449 --> 02:03:52.237
you don't have to wait until the next election, right? Our hands fit so easily

02:03:52.737 --> 02:03:56.235
around their throats. Drag them out. While these comments

02:03:56.735 --> 02:03:59.783
and messages are extremely disturbing and violent, I don't

02:04:00.283 --> 02:04:03.926
care about these people on the internet. I care about the people

02:04:03.958 --> 02:04:07.282
of Eagle Mountain. I always have and I always will.

02:04:07.812 --> 02:04:10.734
And yes, sometimes that means I get choked up and I cry. Why?

02:04:11.103 --> 02:04:15.037
Because I care. And I get that these decisions that we make have an impact

02:04:15.537 --> 02:04:19.205
on real people. I care about the family of 8 that has cut nearly everything

02:04:19.319 --> 02:04:22.623
from their budget. I care about the families managing type

02:04:23.123 --> 02:04:26.935
1 diabetes, seniors on fixed incomes, people working second

02:04:27.435 --> 02:04:30.762
jobs, and parents whose adult children have to move back home.

02:04:31.151 --> 02:04:34.484
Those are the people that I care about. At the

02:04:34.984 --> 02:04:38.370
same time, I'm incredibly grateful for those at the state level,

02:04:38.531 --> 02:04:41.337
like Representative Grecious and Senator Balderry,

02:04:41.996 --> 02:04:45.272
who have reached out to offer solutions and ideas. I'm grateful to

02:04:45.368 --> 02:04:49.398
those who have called me and simply asked, why? How did we

02:04:49.898 --> 02:04:53.268
get here? What can I do to help? If you have an idea that helps

02:04:53.332 --> 02:04:56.881
us meet our needs while leaving more money in the pockets of our

02:04:57.381 --> 02:05:00.638
residents, I want to hear it. And despite what it feels like,

02:05:01.360 --> 02:05:05.294
we have been listening, but that listening started long before the

02:05:05.794 --> 02:05:09.131
public hearing on the 6th. Our mayor and

02:05:09.631 --> 02:05:13.641
council have spent over 62 hours meeting with residents in neighborhood parks,

02:05:14.203 --> 02:05:17.942
HOA clubhouses, plus more than 40 hours at community events.

02:05:18.536 --> 02:05:22.292
We've read hundreds of emails and thousands of comments. Residents told

02:05:22.792 --> 02:05:26.368
us, build roads, address traffic, make it safer

02:05:26.384 --> 02:05:30.011
for our kids to get to school, enforce speeding, take care

02:05:30.511 --> 02:05:34.233
of the parks, keep water and sewer ahead of growth. improve city

02:05:34.522 --> 02:05:38.168
services at City Hall, and make sure deputies are available when

02:05:38.200 --> 02:05:41.959
people need them. Then this year, Chief Knutson told us

02:05:41.975 --> 02:05:45.717
calls for service increased by 18.6% in

02:05:45.750 --> 02:05:50.134
one year and described our staffing as fragile in a city approaching

02:05:50.167 --> 02:05:52.945
80,000 people across 52 square miles.

02:05:53.700 --> 02:05:57.282
The Sheriff's Office identified a need for 10 additional positions.

02:05:57.876 --> 02:06:01.410
We reduced that to 7 because we are already trying to balance that

02:06:01.910 --> 02:06:05.018
need With affordability. And then the residents told

02:06:05.518 --> 02:06:09.142
us something else. The residents said, we understand

02:06:09.642 --> 02:06:13.343
there's a need, but we can't afford this. We heard that too.

02:06:15.392 --> 02:06:18.782
There have been concerns that we haven't been transparent.

02:06:19.408 --> 02:06:23.216
We are imperfect people. None of this current

02:06:23.329 --> 02:06:27.057
mayor and council have ever been through truth and taxation before.

02:06:27.823 --> 02:06:30.860
We should have communicated some things better,

02:06:31.760 --> 02:06:34.459
but our budgets, audits, agendas,

02:06:34.877 --> 02:06:37.849
contracts, and spending decisions are public.

02:06:38.572 --> 02:06:42.091
Every decision about city money is made in a public meeting.

02:06:42.927 --> 02:06:47.008
What I have learned is that making information public isn't enough

02:06:47.731 --> 02:06:51.860
if it's difficult for residents to find or understand.

02:06:52.326 --> 02:06:56.079
We need to do better there. I also want to address

02:06:56.465 --> 02:07:00.185
the claim that we chose data centers over residents. We didn't.

02:07:00.813 --> 02:07:04.735
Data centers have always been a means to an end, a way to bring infrastructure

02:07:05.011 --> 02:07:08.491
and a commercial tax base into Eagle Mountain so residents don't have

02:07:08.991 --> 02:07:12.714
to carry the entire burden. And tonight

02:07:13.135 --> 02:07:16.955
I'm calling on our data centers and our major businesses in Eagle Mountain to step

02:07:17.455 --> 02:07:21.662
up too. Eagle Mountain has welcomed you and provided opportunities

02:07:21.758 --> 02:07:25.269
for you to build your businesses here. Now we need you to

02:07:25.301 --> 02:07:28.636
believe in Eagle Mountain and invest in the people who live

02:07:28.668 --> 02:07:32.435
here. We need good partners. Help us build the

02:07:32.935 --> 02:07:35.657
community that has helped make your investment possible.

02:07:36.828 --> 02:07:40.258
To our residents, I have 2 asks. First, tell us

02:07:40.354 --> 02:07:43.561
what matters most. What can wait? We have

02:07:43.577 --> 02:07:47.328
more than 100 projects and needs Roads, school safety,

02:07:47.408 --> 02:07:50.808
water, sewer, parks, and public safety. If we spend less,

02:07:51.530 --> 02:07:55.298
something has to wait. Tell us what you want

02:07:55.427 --> 02:07:58.762
us to protect. And my second ask is bigger.

02:07:59.997 --> 02:08:03.381
My second ask is take care of each other. I've lived

02:08:03.881 --> 02:08:07.871
here nearly 2 decades. I've watched Eagle Mountain show up when basements have flooded,

02:08:08.496 --> 02:08:11.752
when homes have burned, when someone's child ended up at Primary

02:08:11.800 --> 02:08:15.487
Children's. I've watched neighbors bring meals, fix homes,

02:08:15.908 --> 02:08:18.502
watch children give rides, and quietly help people who needed it.

02:08:19.290 --> 02:08:22.746
Whatever we decide tonight, there will still be people

02:08:22.811 --> 02:08:27.282
struggling tomorrow. So look around, please find

02:08:27.782 --> 02:08:31.237
them, help where you can. And as for my

02:08:31.737 --> 02:08:35.295
vote, I won't make it because someone threatened me. I won't make

02:08:35.795 --> 02:08:39.087
it because somebody praised me. I won't make it based on whether or not it

02:08:39.587 --> 02:08:43.382
helps me get elected again. I have to listen to the people of Eagle Mountain,

02:08:43.913 --> 02:08:46.971
all of the people of Eagle Mountain. I have to look at the facts in

02:08:47.471 --> 02:08:51.272
front of me, understand the consequences, and vote for what I believe is

02:08:51.369 --> 02:08:54.909
right for this community as a whole. Whatever happens

02:08:54.925 --> 02:08:57.818
tonight, tomorrow will still all be neighbors.

02:09:03.528 --> 02:09:06.185
Really? You expect me to follow that, Councilmember Clark?

02:09:08.208 --> 02:09:10.916
I didn't, I didn't write the oration that you did, but I will,

02:09:11.208 --> 02:09:14.872
but I will, but I will simply say this. I agree 100% with what you

02:09:15.372 --> 02:09:17.977
stated. Uh,

02:09:20.790 --> 02:09:24.691
I think the biggest regret that I have in this process is that

02:09:25.191 --> 02:09:28.803
we did not communicate effectively. I'm a terrible communicator. I can talk to

02:09:29.303 --> 02:09:32.963
you one-on-one, but I am not the public face of anything. In fact,

02:09:32.979 --> 02:09:34.844
I shun that. It's not, it's not my personality.

02:09:36.539 --> 02:09:40.142
And I think that's where we have failed pretty miserably. Let me, let me restate

02:09:40.191 --> 02:09:43.450
that. That's where I have failed miserably. Let me take responsibility

02:09:43.466 --> 02:09:46.678
for myself and not for others. Um,

02:09:48.008 --> 02:09:50.810
I wish I had a do-over and could, and could, uh,

02:09:53.286 --> 02:09:56.910
more effectively communicate to more people those things

02:09:57.410 --> 02:09:59.830
that we have been dealing with. I think Councilmember Clark just gave you a brief

02:09:59.846 --> 02:10:02.064
synopsis of some of the things we've been dealing with. Thank you.

02:10:03.794 --> 02:10:07.095
This is not fun. This affects me. It affects my mother.

02:10:07.159 --> 02:10:10.524
It affects my sister. It affects my daughter. It affects my son. It affects my

02:10:11.024 --> 02:10:14.130
grandchildren who live here in the city. The easiest thing to

02:10:14.630 --> 02:10:17.736
say is we're not going to do anything, and the data centers can take

02:10:18.236 --> 02:10:21.085
care of all of it at some point in time. But the reality of it

02:10:21.585 --> 02:10:25.139
is, I want to make sure that our city grows and prospers, and that

02:10:25.171 --> 02:10:28.553
we're meeting today's needs while planning for tomorrow's. Outcomes.

02:10:29.819 --> 02:10:33.939
Um, I didn't come to office to do anything but

02:10:33.987 --> 02:10:37.498
to see if I couldn't help improve the circumstance that we found ourselves

02:10:37.594 --> 02:10:41.265
in. That's it. I don't have any, any goals

02:10:41.297 --> 02:10:44.583
beyond that. Um, it was a wrestle for me to want

02:10:45.083 --> 02:10:49.056
to even serve a second term. It's not a fun job.

02:10:49.248 --> 02:10:52.117
It's not enjoyable. It's a heavy lift.

02:10:53.544 --> 02:10:57.115
And, uh, It's weighty. Somebody needs to

02:10:57.615 --> 02:10:59.786
do it, and I felt like I had something to contribute. And let me tell

02:11:00.286 --> 02:11:02.329
you some of the things that have been accomplished while I have sat here.

02:11:03.302 --> 02:11:06.593
We've adjusted residential codes so that the spacing in front of

02:11:07.093 --> 02:11:11.013
your houses is wider and larger than it used to be. We've made road

02:11:11.046 --> 02:11:13.661
standards wider and bigger than they used to be.

02:11:16.108 --> 02:11:20.294
We, we, we have reduced the number of developed

02:11:20.794 --> 02:11:25.082
units that were approved by Previous councils who at the time made those decisions.

02:11:25.147 --> 02:11:28.357
I'm certain that they were the right decisions in the time frame that they dealt

02:11:28.857 --> 02:11:32.706
with, but they couldn't have possibly seen the impact or the outcome that

02:11:32.786 --> 02:11:34.472
we are now dealing with today.

02:11:35.916 --> 02:11:39.062
I personally have helped to work and reduce the number of units in our

02:11:39.562 --> 02:11:43.235
city by several thousand units. I've personally done that.

02:11:44.037 --> 02:11:48.022
I'm the one who stood among this council and said This council

02:11:48.522 --> 02:11:51.913
in the past counseled and said we cannot continue to sell our water

02:11:52.413 --> 02:11:55.752
resources for residential development. And we made that

02:11:56.252 --> 02:11:59.898
adjustment. My desire has been to

02:12:00.398 --> 02:12:04.124
serve you and to produce outcomes that will benefit

02:12:04.317 --> 02:12:08.607
you and me long term. I believe

02:12:09.107 --> 02:12:10.454
that a tax increase is necessary.

02:12:11.965 --> 02:12:15.350
Perhaps we overshot the mark. I'm going to just say that publicly.

02:12:15.590 --> 02:12:19.307
Okay, but I'm going to tell you, no matter where things

02:12:19.339 --> 02:12:22.591
land, there are way more needs than

02:12:22.623 --> 02:12:26.228
there will be resources to fill them. And I listened

02:12:26.728 --> 02:12:29.817
to the gentleman who just spoke about the 3 stop signs, and he's going to

02:12:30.317 --> 02:12:32.925
go put them up himself. We shouldn't ever have to get to a place where

02:12:32.957 --> 02:12:35.601
that's the only recourse that we have, should we?

02:12:37.043 --> 02:12:40.039
And so to hear that is very frustrating to me, not from you, sir.

02:12:40.167 --> 02:12:42.811
I don't, I don't blame you. I understand where you're coming from. I've met with

02:12:43.311 --> 02:12:46.293
you. And I've seen what you're dealing with. And if you,

02:12:47.309 --> 02:12:50.778
if you're aware, I'm the one who stood up in a council meeting in the

02:12:51.278 --> 02:12:55.048
budget and said, we need to allocate some resources to put in some speed tables

02:12:55.081 --> 02:12:58.291
or some sort of speed calming measures in front of our elementary schools.

02:12:59.053 --> 02:13:00.398
But we had to find that money somewhere.

02:13:02.152 --> 02:13:05.540
So I hope that you'll give us a little grace.

02:13:07.799 --> 02:13:11.776
Challenges. I'm okay with that. Have a difference of opinion. There's no issues

02:13:11.825 --> 02:13:14.138
with that whatsoever, but talk to us,

02:13:14.652 --> 02:13:18.137
engage us, and engage me. I'm happy to

02:13:18.185 --> 02:13:21.607
have a conversation, a phone call, a text, an email. I will engage

02:13:21.719 --> 02:13:25.783
with you. Facebook and some of the cesspools that exist in our— in

02:13:25.831 --> 02:13:29.879
our— and I'm going to call it just that— our Eagle Mountain Citizens page.

02:13:30.377 --> 02:13:34.023
I call it Eagle Mountain Citizens cesspool, and I truly believe that.

02:13:34.650 --> 02:13:38.506
Now, Many of you will disagree with that, but for me, it's not a market

02:13:39.006 --> 02:13:41.574
that I want to spend a lot of time in because there's so much hate

02:13:41.622 --> 02:13:44.965
and vitriol that exists there. And it's not how

02:13:45.095 --> 02:13:48.495
I live my life. I want to live my life better than that.

02:13:48.980 --> 02:13:52.785
Thank you. I'll just

02:13:53.285 --> 02:13:57.109
say ditto to both the comments that have already been made by

02:13:57.401 --> 02:13:59.879
Councilmembers Clark and Wright.

02:14:01.063 --> 02:14:05.236
And I'll just add just briefly to some other comments. We met with Congressman

02:14:05.736 --> 02:14:09.553
Mike Kennedy this last week, a few of us did, and he said something profound

02:14:10.053 --> 02:14:13.951
that opened my eyes a bit. You know, he works at the federal level and

02:14:14.384 --> 02:14:17.803
confirmed what we already know, that we need to minimize

02:14:17.819 --> 02:14:20.580
the amount of money that goes to the federal level. There's so much waste that

02:14:21.080 --> 02:14:24.881
happens there. And he said we need to reduce the

02:14:25.381 --> 02:14:28.891
money that goes to the federal level. He said, similarly, the state, there's, there's ways

02:14:28.987 --> 02:14:33.182
we can improve the efficiency there and

02:14:33.262 --> 02:14:35.973
reduce the amount of money that's going to the state. And then here's where he

02:14:36.473 --> 02:14:38.535
said the eye-opening remark. But to the cities,

02:14:40.310 --> 02:14:43.513
to the cities, you need to make sure that the

02:14:44.013 --> 02:14:47.477
taxes are there. That is where the people

02:14:47.977 --> 02:14:50.628
will feel it. It goes directly to them.

02:14:52.033 --> 02:14:55.813
It builds them. You got to make sure

02:14:56.313 --> 02:15:00.205
that the taxes don't lag behind, because then the cities

02:15:00.237 --> 02:15:03.602
will fail. That is where the taxes

02:15:03.700 --> 02:15:07.229
should be higher, and the federal and the state as low as possible.

02:15:08.492 --> 02:15:11.919
This is the money that's being raised to help us,

02:15:12.760 --> 02:15:16.123
our city, the future generations that come after us.

02:15:16.657 --> 02:15:21.049
This is where the taxes. when there's an increase should

02:15:21.549 --> 02:15:25.257
be considered and acknowledged that that is coming as an investment

02:15:25.289 --> 02:15:28.374
here. And I realize, like, I've lived many years of

02:15:28.874 --> 02:15:32.165
my life in very, very challenging financial circumstances.

02:15:33.000 --> 02:15:36.325
I remember coming out of my house one day and my neighbor across the

02:15:36.358 --> 02:15:39.586
street was getting in his car and said, hey, where are you

02:15:40.086 --> 02:15:42.221
going, Keith? And he said, well, I'm going to Cafe Rio. You want to— you

02:15:42.721 --> 02:15:45.369
want to go with me? Back then, the Cafe Rio burrito was like $6.

02:15:45.900 --> 02:15:49.828
There's inflation since then, but I couldn't go. I couldn't afford

02:15:49.860 --> 02:15:52.506
that. There are times in my life where I skipped meals in order to make

02:15:53.006 --> 02:15:55.200
sure there was enough money in the family. I understand what that is.

02:15:56.354 --> 02:15:59.882
We're tasked with hearing, and that some have said,

02:15:59.946 --> 02:16:03.297
well, that council, you haven't heard us because of various things.

02:16:04.372 --> 02:16:08.268
Councilmember Clark just outlined very well the competing voices

02:16:08.284 --> 02:16:11.683
that are coming to us from you saying we have, we have

02:16:11.732 --> 02:16:15.517
needs for better roads. Uh, better improve public

02:16:16.017 --> 02:16:19.096
safety and a whole list of things. All of that costs money.

02:16:20.557 --> 02:16:23.574
All of that costs money. Then we're hearing from some residents,

02:16:24.007 --> 02:16:27.297
I'm struggling right now financially. There's a balancing act that

02:16:27.797 --> 02:16:31.277
we have to do in that. And yes, this is the first— our first time

02:16:31.325 --> 02:16:33.796
going through this tax and truth and taxation process.

02:16:34.358 --> 02:16:37.519
There are some state laws that regulate how the communications

02:16:37.584 --> 02:16:41.082
come out, but in retrospect, we, we, we evaluate and

02:16:41.114 --> 02:16:44.370
think, okay, we for sure could have improved. I'm, I'm really,

02:16:44.386 --> 02:16:47.514
really proud of the 2 council members. I'm proud of all the council members

02:16:48.014 --> 02:16:51.621
here, but the council members to our left, Wood and Hewish, have already

02:16:51.685 --> 02:16:55.470
created code to improve the transparency of property

02:16:55.970 --> 02:16:59.272
tax dollars in the city. It was discussed in our workshop session,

02:16:59.416 --> 02:17:02.913
so it should be coming back to a policy session soon. That's how fast they

02:17:02.994 --> 02:17:06.779
acted to improve both the transparency and ensure that the property

02:17:07.279 --> 02:17:10.661
tax dollars are indeed 100% going to public safety. And I'm proud of how

02:17:10.693 --> 02:17:14.143
fast they acted. Thank you for coming. Thank you for

02:17:14.643 --> 02:17:18.174
the numerous residents who have reached out. Every one of you that has emailed me,

02:17:18.559 --> 02:17:21.610
you know this, every one of you got an email back. Every single

02:17:22.110 --> 02:17:24.757
one of you. I've stayed up really late some nights to make sure everyone got

02:17:25.257 --> 02:17:28.578
responded to that reached out to me. And, and I will continue to do those—

02:17:28.771 --> 02:17:31.468
that to those who reach out. Thank you for your information,

02:17:31.565 --> 02:17:34.246
participation, and your energy in helping improve our city.

02:17:39.495 --> 02:17:42.600
I'm grateful you're all here, and I truly mean that.

02:17:42.648 --> 02:17:45.720
I think you know that I, I don't shy away from people coming here to

02:17:46.220 --> 02:17:49.488
tell us how we can be better. I do have some,

02:17:49.860 --> 02:17:53.337
some disappointments in the last couple months. Um,

02:17:55.245 --> 02:17:58.741
I love living here, and I, I've told my family a thousand times I have

02:17:59.241 --> 02:18:02.257
zero desire to ever leave this area. I love the people here.

02:18:02.630 --> 02:18:06.285
I love the community here. I don't think our best foot was forward the last

02:18:06.785 --> 02:18:10.244
couple months. We didn't put a very good look

02:18:10.744 --> 02:18:14.010
on Eagle Mountain, frankly, and a lot of other people took advantage of that

02:18:14.059 --> 02:18:15.487
and made it even worse in the media.

02:18:18.087 --> 02:18:21.405
And I'm gonna own part of that. I mean, frankly, we didn't, we didn't

02:18:21.905 --> 02:18:23.785
help you to understand better. That's on us.

02:18:24.886 --> 02:18:27.577
I'm not even gonna make the excuse that this is our first time around.

02:18:27.723 --> 02:18:31.643
We know that we have some communication challenges. And frankly,

02:18:31.692 --> 02:18:33.946
I'm gonna tell you, I don't think social media is really cutting it.

02:18:35.009 --> 02:18:39.083
There are so many people that are not even utilizing that for their communication,

02:18:39.598 --> 02:18:42.093
and even if they do, the algorithm might not even be touching them.

02:18:43.445 --> 02:18:47.502
So we want to figure out how

02:18:47.566 --> 02:18:49.981
to get the information to you in a way that works.

02:18:51.686 --> 02:18:57.260
As Councilmember Whiting mentioned, Councilmember Hewish and I have

02:18:57.760 --> 02:19:01.194
been talking about how to bracket and put a good financial

02:19:01.694 --> 02:19:05.224
plan in place so that when we're done, the next council can

02:19:05.724 --> 02:19:07.648
come in here and we left it better than we, than we found it.

02:19:08.660 --> 02:19:12.385
I think that we are— we're close with that first part

02:19:12.885 --> 02:19:16.062
of the code, and it will absolutely do exactly what we told you it would

02:19:16.562 --> 02:19:19.835
do. It forces it to go to a separate account for

02:19:20.335 --> 02:19:24.795
property taxes to be Put for public safety only, and that'll be delineated

02:19:25.295 --> 02:19:29.000
in the account. So you have absolute confidence that that money is

02:19:29.049 --> 02:19:32.708
only going towards that. The second thing is to know when

02:19:33.221 --> 02:19:36.849
property taxes should be even reviewed, and honestly, it probably ought to

02:19:37.349 --> 02:19:40.075
be yearly, and that's kind of what we put in there. It's,

02:19:41.503 --> 02:19:45.323
it's very easy to point fingers backwards, you know, and I'm

02:19:45.355 --> 02:19:48.485
not going to say that I haven't done that because I have. And I don't

02:19:48.985 --> 02:19:51.373
know all the reasons that these things weren't done. All I can say is that

02:19:51.873 --> 02:19:55.482
now we can't make any excuses for why we don't have financial plans.

02:19:56.509 --> 02:19:59.944
It's good governance to have financial plans so that we can plan how we use

02:20:00.444 --> 02:20:04.148
the money. We need to have what we do now. We need to have

02:20:04.648 --> 02:20:06.989
a 5-year. We need to have a 10-year, and even further down the road,

02:20:07.085 --> 02:20:10.472
20-year. Our intent, I can tell you, one of the

02:20:10.972 --> 02:20:14.194
reasons that I was so adamant about appointing Mr.

02:20:14.242 --> 02:20:18.697
Hewish is because of his financial background, because I believe we need his expertise,

02:20:18.793 --> 02:20:22.191
and he has shown that in droves of why he's been

02:20:22.691 --> 02:20:25.780
so beneficial. Our intent is to do better,

02:20:26.598 --> 02:20:30.027
to make it more transparent, and I— the reality

02:20:30.527 --> 02:20:33.456
of it is, is I wish that we would have been doing incremental increases so

02:20:33.956 --> 02:20:37.206
we're not sitting facing what we're facing. But I think Councilmember Clark made one

02:20:37.318 --> 02:20:40.683
important point. About— you

02:20:41.183 --> 02:20:45.587
have to decide what it is you want to cut out. Because the

02:20:46.087 --> 02:20:49.267
cost of things are so incredibly high right now. I actually asked one of the

02:20:49.767 --> 02:20:52.834
things to be pulled off our consent agenda because I want you to see what

02:20:53.334 --> 02:20:57.333
the cost of one single thing for our sewer plant is going to cost.

02:20:57.960 --> 02:21:02.154
Because I think it's very easy to not absorb

02:21:02.299 --> 02:21:05.210
the cost of everything. When you start taking a look at what each of these

02:21:05.242 --> 02:21:08.793
projects cost, We have to leverage small amounts

02:21:09.293 --> 02:21:13.142
of money into larger amounts of money by making payments, because we don't have the

02:21:13.642 --> 02:21:16.469
income to take care of what our total needs are. If you look at our

02:21:16.969 --> 02:21:20.329
total projects, uh, just for roads, I think I mentioned this the

02:21:20.829 --> 02:21:23.617
last time, our sole responsibility is $419 million.

02:21:25.353 --> 02:21:29.277
The total projects are like $1.5 billion for roads

02:21:29.552 --> 02:21:32.685
where we have the state, MAG, and other sources that are

02:21:33.185 --> 02:21:36.918
paying for them. That's Eagle Mountain. It's astounding when

02:21:36.967 --> 02:21:39.408
you get into this and you find out what everything costs.

02:21:40.179 --> 02:21:43.536
That was the, you know, the wall that hit me in the face of what

02:21:43.633 --> 02:21:45.737
things are actually costing and what our resources are.

02:21:46.925 --> 02:21:49.335
I want to start with that because I think that that's important for you to

02:21:49.835 --> 02:21:53.126
share the burden with us as we're trying to evaluate how we solve some of

02:21:53.626 --> 02:21:56.740
these problems, because we are really talking about building roads.

02:21:57.527 --> 02:22:01.076
We drive on the same crappy traffic that all the rest of you

02:22:01.576 --> 02:22:05.299
do. And each one of us live along that way where it's super crappy.

02:22:05.508 --> 02:22:08.928
In fact, I, I'm right where it gets really, really crappy in Silver Lake.

02:22:09.731 --> 02:22:12.910
And I— there's sometimes we can't even leave the neighborhood because it is lined all

02:22:12.958 --> 02:22:15.334
the way back to Hidden Valley.

02:22:16.266 --> 02:22:19.702
So I just— I'm asking for a little bit of grace

02:22:20.202 --> 02:22:23.893
from you. Understand that there's nobody here that's trying to harm anybody. We're trying

02:22:24.393 --> 02:22:27.409
to come up with a solution. I don't know that we found the,

02:22:27.810 --> 02:22:31.070
the perfect solution, but we're doing our best to try to find some way to

02:22:31.102 --> 02:22:34.297
be able to attack some of these projects that have to get taken care of.

02:22:35.196 --> 02:22:38.697
Roads being probably at the very top of that. One of our other problems,

02:22:38.729 --> 02:22:42.277
though, and I'm just going to be totally honest with you, we are undermanned.

02:22:42.984 --> 02:22:45.970
We do not have enough people to do the projects.

02:22:47.159 --> 02:22:49.808
That is one of those— you ask, what would you have done with the extra

02:22:50.308 --> 02:22:54.194
money? For me personally, it would have absolutely been bringing

02:22:54.226 --> 02:22:57.761
in teams of people for roads and parks to be able to take

02:22:58.261 --> 02:23:01.585
care of our assets. That's my personal opinion. I'm not all 5 of

02:23:01.617 --> 02:23:04.429
us, but I just think it's important for you to know how we're weighing our

02:23:04.929 --> 02:23:08.767
decisions. I want to be truthful with you always. I've always been that way.

02:23:09.892 --> 02:23:12.446
You're not always going to like what I say, but I will always tell you

02:23:12.946 --> 02:23:16.351
the truth. Thank you for being here. I appreciate it. I'm looking forward to your

02:23:16.463 --> 02:23:20.342
comments. I ask that you help us come up with some solutions. Be creative,

02:23:20.927 --> 02:23:23.206
because I think we're all in this together. Thanks.

02:23:27.465 --> 02:23:31.177
So, there was a shout out that a citizen wanted me to provide, and I'll

02:23:31.677 --> 02:23:35.282
keep the citizen's name confidential. But this is a shout out to our Sheriff's Department.

02:23:35.330 --> 02:23:38.856
So, the Eagle Mountain Division of the Sheriff Department, specifically Deputy

02:23:38.969 --> 02:23:42.257
Craig— no, no relation to me, by the way, but he's

02:23:42.757 --> 02:23:46.194
got good names. Yeah, specifically Deputy Craig. Has been

02:23:46.227 --> 02:23:49.857
phenomenal in helping us. Will you please give Deputy Craig a shout

02:23:50.357 --> 02:23:53.810
out? We absolutely 100% love this guy. He has helped my

02:23:54.310 --> 02:23:54.601
family a lot.

02:23:58.808 --> 02:24:02.177
Okay, I'll be fast. I first just want to thank

02:24:02.193 --> 02:24:06.336
everybody who's reached out to me individually. I've been just going one

02:24:06.465 --> 02:24:09.814
by one, two by two, Zoom meetings, phone calls.

02:24:10.635 --> 02:24:14.080
I've created a presentation, and one of the first slides

02:24:14.177 --> 02:24:15.529
in that presentation—those of you, I'm sorry if you haven't seen the matrix.

02:24:18.006 --> 02:24:21.727
It's probably my favorite movie of all time. But, in the beginning of

02:24:22.227 --> 02:24:26.143
the movie, the main character, he's given the choice to choose between

02:24:26.240 --> 02:24:29.478
taking the blue pill, which he wakes up and he goes

02:24:29.511 --> 02:24:33.421
back to his regular life. Nothing changes.

02:24:34.165 --> 02:24:37.740
The other pill, the red pill, he takes and he learns that he's actually

02:24:38.240 --> 02:24:41.509
not living in reality at all and he gets unplugged from the system and realizes

02:24:41.590 --> 02:24:44.176
that society ended 200 years ago.

02:24:45.156 --> 02:24:48.772
Serving on city council is like taking the red

02:24:48.836 --> 02:24:52.500
pill. My eyes have completely been opened. I've been

02:24:53.000 --> 02:24:56.625
learning about government accounting, finances,

02:24:56.803 --> 02:25:00.347
how things work and operate, that we don't have a cell tower in our city.

02:25:01.115 --> 02:25:05.108
We had a visitor here, billion-dollar investor

02:25:05.608 --> 02:25:09.679
looking to come to Eagle Mountain that we're aggressively recruiting commercial. And he's

02:25:10.179 --> 02:25:13.622
like, oh, I don't have any cell service here. And I'm like, yeah, that's not,

02:25:13.735 --> 02:25:16.748
not great. Um, but okay. Uh,

02:25:17.678 --> 02:25:21.429
I just, I want to just extend appreciation. There's a few

02:25:21.929 --> 02:25:25.324
people here today that I've met with in a 1-on-1, and I'm grateful to

02:25:25.356 --> 02:25:28.739
have all of you. So, while I have you now, I probably won't

02:25:29.239 --> 02:25:32.538
post this on Facebook because everything just gets distorted and

02:25:32.586 --> 02:25:35.840
the comments get crazy. I prefer just a 1-on-1. I'm— Much

02:25:35.937 --> 02:25:39.535
like Brett. Okay. Um, so one of the pieces,

02:25:39.808 --> 02:25:42.780
and there will probably be 4 or 5 more things that I think we could

02:25:43.280 --> 02:25:46.844
do to improve this process, is as a city council, when you come in

02:25:46.876 --> 02:25:50.185
brand new, uh, you, you have some presentations.

02:25:50.249 --> 02:25:53.494
We, we had one from the, from, uh, Chief Knutson

02:25:53.767 --> 02:25:58.024
that says we need more sheriffs. And, uh, what do I know? I'm a financial

02:25:58.040 --> 02:26:00.995
planner. I don't know how many sheriffs we need. And, and so you try to

02:26:01.028 --> 02:26:03.437
dig into the data as good as you can. Yeah.

02:26:04.927 --> 02:26:08.516
And what we have strived, or at least started to work toward,

02:26:08.533 --> 02:26:12.730
is having some kind of safety net for our sheriff's contract,

02:26:12.778 --> 02:26:15.999
and maybe one day a police department. That,

02:26:16.079 --> 02:26:19.316
that's a really interesting idea to have land to build our own jail.

02:26:20.646 --> 02:26:23.882
But the goal of this code that we're putting in place

02:26:24.154 --> 02:26:27.375
is to require a council each year to look

02:26:27.875 --> 02:26:31.301
at the coverage ratio of our property taxes. So when you pay a property

02:26:31.801 --> 02:26:35.983
tax, Number 1, there will be a dedicated segregated

02:26:36.048 --> 02:26:39.816
fund that those dollars cannot be commingled with sales tax.

02:26:40.412 --> 02:26:43.501
So when you look at your city property tax that you pay,

02:26:44.263 --> 02:26:47.811
every dollar goes directly to our safety.

02:26:50.086 --> 02:26:53.982
If the coverage ratio target is in this code, it'll be 85%.

02:26:54.063 --> 02:26:57.361
That'll be the target. We may not get there this year. I don't know.

02:26:57.441 --> 02:27:00.710
We'll have to to see where we, where we land this evening. There will

02:27:01.210 --> 02:27:04.668
be an upper band. If the coverage ratio is above 95%,

02:27:05.197 --> 02:27:08.386
then a city council could consider cutting taxes.

02:27:09.123 --> 02:27:13.273
If it's below the lower band, the city council could consider increasing

02:27:13.305 --> 02:27:17.648
taxes. But the goal is that each year city councils are

02:27:18.097 --> 02:27:21.879
looking at this coverage ratio so we don't get in a position where we're

02:27:22.379 --> 02:27:25.536
behind and new revenue coming in is subsidizing those

02:27:25.568 --> 02:27:28.875
contracts. As data centers complete

02:27:29.375 --> 02:27:33.529
their projects and those properties have values and can be assessed

02:27:34.029 --> 02:27:36.980
a property tax, that obviously is going to increase the property tax number.

02:27:37.703 --> 02:27:40.544
So that, that's one of the directions that we're heading.

02:27:41.058 --> 02:27:45.054
Another one that we're talking about is having just

02:27:45.554 --> 02:27:49.179
a very simple, straightforward budget that residents could easily flip

02:27:49.228 --> 02:27:52.501
through and say, okay, I understand what our city budget is. Going through

02:27:52.533 --> 02:27:56.459
100 pages of documents. I went to our city website over the

02:27:56.959 --> 02:28:00.048
weekend and I spent a few hours. I just said, Zach, pretend like you don't

02:28:00.548 --> 02:28:04.070
know anything and you're just reading our city budget and you see a

02:28:04.570 --> 02:28:08.397
$50 million transaction. Well, what is that? Well, we have

02:28:08.897 --> 02:28:12.243
a sewer project that we're working on, and there's transfers of funds that

02:28:12.724 --> 02:28:16.089
by state law are required to go from one account to another account. But if

02:28:16.589 --> 02:28:20.479
you don't know anything about Um, the— how government accounting works,

02:28:20.511 --> 02:28:24.501
it might look suspicious. You know, you hear $363

02:28:25.001 --> 02:28:27.930
million. Well, that's plenty of money to do whatever you need to do. Um,

02:28:27.946 --> 02:28:31.279
but really, we have some big major projects. We have a couple wells

02:28:31.295 --> 02:28:34.596
that are being built this next year to create water infrastructure.

02:28:34.981 --> 02:28:38.618
We have a sewer, uh, that, that's being built to create more infrastructure

02:28:39.388 --> 02:28:42.144
and lots of road projects. So, um,

02:28:43.474 --> 02:28:46.715
I would just say, If you'd like to meet individually

02:28:47.215 --> 02:28:50.664
with me, I'd love to visit with you. I welcome that opportunity. I know it's

02:28:51.293 --> 02:28:54.759
not the most convenient thing in the world to establish that time, but I welcome

02:28:55.259 --> 02:28:57.341
that and appreciate everyone being here tonight.

02:28:58.891 --> 02:29:01.894
Thank you. All right, I'll just add a

02:29:01.958 --> 02:29:06.284
couple of real quick comments, and it's maybe a little different direction for

02:29:06.301 --> 02:29:09.674
educational purposes. I was going to do this

02:29:09.739 --> 02:29:12.177
the opposite, but as I think about it, I'm going to, I'm going to switch

02:29:12.209 --> 02:29:15.349
my order. There is no one I would rather be in the trenches with than

02:29:15.381 --> 02:29:18.962
these guys. And trust me, if you think any

02:29:18.994 --> 02:29:22.703
one of us haven't had a battle, I think we had one today. And I'm

02:29:23.203 --> 02:29:25.914
not afraid to say it because we— I can still say that he's one of

02:29:26.414 --> 02:29:29.575
my best friends. We don't have to agree, but we can respect each other and,

02:29:29.752 --> 02:29:32.931
and try to come to a conclusion. I know we've

02:29:33.431 --> 02:29:36.784
had our battles. Every one of us up here have disagreed, and man,

02:29:36.817 --> 02:29:41.537
we have to just Fight through that. And there isn't— it

02:29:42.037 --> 02:29:44.973
even took a couple days to cool down after one of them. One.

02:29:45.535 --> 02:29:49.276
Yeah. I didn't tell him we battle every day. The rest of

02:29:49.776 --> 02:29:53.323
them is just one. It's, uh, it's— and there's

02:29:53.435 --> 02:29:56.695
no one I'd rather do this with. Now, switching gears,

02:29:57.353 --> 02:30:00.099
my, my role is a little bit different. Uh,

02:30:01.207 --> 02:30:04.577
I get asked to go out and get information.

02:30:05.490 --> 02:30:08.887
It doesn't matter what I think. I have to get the information.

02:30:09.160 --> 02:30:11.307
That's one of the reasons I try to get out in front of this and

02:30:11.807 --> 02:30:14.688
give people information. It's not my stance, it's information. I'm trying to give you some

02:30:15.188 --> 02:30:17.877
facts, uh, and then I have to come back and give these guys the information,

02:30:17.893 --> 02:30:20.666
and they got to make the decision. I don't get to say where this lands.

02:30:21.243 --> 02:30:24.784
I have dang sure tried to influence the best I could, but I

02:30:25.284 --> 02:30:29.127
don't get to make this decision. It's my job once the decision is made to

02:30:29.627 --> 02:30:32.590
then Carry it out whether I agree or not. I get to carry that out.

02:30:33.296 --> 02:30:36.054
So what I can tell you is,

02:30:36.663 --> 02:30:40.175
do we all agree? Nope. Are we going to battle it out?

02:30:40.480 --> 02:30:43.382
Yep. And then I'm going to carry it out no matter if I agree with

02:30:43.882 --> 02:30:47.375
it or not. And so that, that's, that's something that I just wanted, that I

02:30:47.875 --> 02:30:50.117
was thinking about, that I, that I would add to, uh, that. And I'm gonna

02:30:50.617 --> 02:30:52.827
leave it at that. The last, the other piece was, uh,

02:30:52.859 --> 02:30:56.307
I'm, I'm never afraid of hard conversations.

02:30:56.836 --> 02:31:00.457
I love calling the people that hate me. And trust me,

02:31:01.562 --> 02:31:04.703
I do it with a smile. And it's not because I'm trying to pick a

02:31:05.203 --> 02:31:08.756
fight. It's because I wanna gain greater understanding and hopefully

02:31:08.788 --> 02:31:12.361
shed some light for you. And maybe on the other end, we can be friends

02:31:12.473 --> 02:31:16.062
because I'm okay with a disagreement as long as we're not disagreeable, as long as

02:31:16.562 --> 02:31:20.356
we do it with respect. And I want to help you understand some

02:31:20.645 --> 02:31:24.570
maybe perspective. With that, I'm going to set records straight

02:31:25.070 --> 02:31:28.982
when I can. It's not a subjective-objective. These are not

02:31:29.482 --> 02:31:32.995
opinions, they're simply facts. So I

02:31:33.059 --> 02:31:36.847
don't like it when people aren't informed, and I'm not saying it's malicious,

02:31:36.863 --> 02:31:40.827
I'm saying it's not right. I sit in meetings every

02:31:40.859 --> 02:31:44.518
single day, and I can tell you, if you want to know

02:31:44.551 --> 02:31:48.964
how many times I've met with our data center partners in the last

02:31:49.464 --> 02:31:52.737
6 months, but even in the last 2 months, Man, I— a

02:31:53.237 --> 02:31:55.563
lot. I'm just going to say that a lot. Um,

02:31:56.735 --> 02:31:59.931
if somebody has information about 25

02:31:59.963 --> 02:32:03.447
to 40 buildings and QTS, I don't. And I

02:32:03.480 --> 02:32:06.772
sit with the people making the decisions, and they haven't even said

02:32:07.272 --> 02:32:10.529
that. So whoever's saying that they've got these multiple approvals,

02:32:11.509 --> 02:32:13.725
they don't even know that, but they appreciate it because they would love that.

02:32:14.158 --> 02:32:17.868
But they have never said that. Also, to continue and

02:32:18.368 --> 02:32:22.073
talk about water. They have less water allocated

02:32:22.573 --> 02:32:26.464
at QTS than one street of houses. They are not using

02:32:26.577 --> 02:32:29.727
water. That is a closed-loop system. You hear us say

02:32:30.227 --> 02:32:33.463
that. I'm not going to get into it. If you want information, look me up.

02:32:33.996 --> 02:32:37.489
They are not using our drinking water on a daily basis. They use

02:32:37.989 --> 02:32:41.624
it for their kitchen and their bathrooms. Happy to have that conversation. Just a fact.

02:32:43.543 --> 02:32:47.190
Um, now, Because of some of the smear that goes

02:32:47.287 --> 02:32:50.730
on, including on Facebook and others, this is not aimed at any person

02:32:51.228 --> 02:32:54.430
or any comment that I'm talking about. I want to shed a little bit of

02:32:54.462 --> 02:32:58.194
light on what those people have done just

02:32:58.694 --> 02:33:01.909
recently. I, 3 weeks ago,

02:33:03.350 --> 02:33:06.657
was, uh, and I'm not gonna say who it was even. I was going

02:33:06.689 --> 02:33:09.028
to. I'm not going to say this. I was in a meeting with some of

02:33:09.528 --> 02:33:13.576
our employees that said, hey, The next phase of QTS,

02:33:13.960 --> 02:33:17.293
they're not asking for any tax breaks. They will

02:33:17.325 --> 02:33:20.450
be built next year with no asks,

02:33:20.546 --> 02:33:24.184
100% taxpayer day 1. I read in the meeting

02:33:24.312 --> 02:33:27.565
on August 6th those numbers. I'm not going to read them again.

02:33:27.837 --> 02:33:31.106
Look it up back there. It was $19 million that they

02:33:31.606 --> 02:33:34.263
will have in. It takes time for that to come in. That will be a

02:33:34.763 --> 02:33:38.750
taxable value next year, 0 break. That's a

02:33:38.895 --> 02:33:42.406
good deal. That's what we've been waiting for. Now,

02:33:42.743 --> 02:33:45.917
knowing that, as a staff internally,

02:33:45.949 --> 02:33:49.316
we're like, hey, we have some needs. Maybe if they would front

02:33:49.816 --> 02:33:53.325
some money, we could give them back some, a little bit of tax just

02:33:53.825 --> 02:33:56.259
to cover our need, tie it directly to that. Then they're still full taxpayer.

02:33:57.253 --> 02:34:00.444
I said, no, I'm not okay with that. And I want you

02:34:00.944 --> 02:34:03.202
guys to know what I said. And then I brought it to these guys because

02:34:03.702 --> 02:34:06.874
I don't have the power to do that. And I said, I'm gonna make a

02:34:07.374 --> 02:34:09.749
phone call. I got on the phone with QTS and I said, hey,

02:34:10.648 --> 02:34:12.976
that's crap. I'm not paying for this road. You guys are the ones that are

02:34:13.476 --> 02:34:16.830
making it bad. And that intersection over there, you're the ones doing that.

02:34:17.456 --> 02:34:20.057
At best, you have to pay for those lights and split the road.

02:34:20.844 --> 02:34:24.119
He said, let me call you back. Within a day, he called

02:34:24.619 --> 02:34:27.668
me back and said, where do you want the check? And I said, we estimate

02:34:28.168 --> 02:34:31.377
it's about $5 million. He said, if it's $5.5 million, we're paying for that road.

02:34:31.842 --> 02:34:34.873
And I'm telling you right now, that road's getting built because of QTS,

02:34:35.451 --> 02:34:39.380
no strings attached. And the signal? And the signal,

02:34:39.444 --> 02:34:43.084
2 signals. 2 signals. So, to sit here and

02:34:43.584 --> 02:34:46.677
say these guys suck, I'm not okay with that. I'm not.

02:34:47.302 --> 02:34:51.295
So, I will tell you that I'm also continuing

02:34:51.328 --> 02:34:53.942
to work with both of our data center partners that are already built and those

02:34:53.974 --> 02:34:57.101
that are approved to continue to help us bridge these gaps.

02:34:57.743 --> 02:35:01.420
And so we are continually— and they are stepping up. That's my

02:35:01.920 --> 02:35:05.482
commitment. So I just won't allow for that

02:35:05.611 --> 02:35:09.336
to, to be a narrative that's out there without

02:35:09.384 --> 02:35:12.258
saying the other side. Now, what I will allow is you can say you disagree

