02:52:40.069 --> 02:52:43.785
say, if you like the discussion, then, then that'll save

02:52:43.801 --> 02:52:46.045
us all some time. So that's why it's here, and that's where we're at.

02:52:46.751 --> 02:52:50.838
Um, so let me, let me start. I mean, the first item, Mayor, is 13A,

02:52:50.854 --> 02:52:54.654
right? And it's really the question of whether or not we're going to repeal the

02:52:55.154 --> 02:52:57.770
property tax increase certified rate that we approved on August 6th.

02:52:58.702 --> 02:53:02.701
And I've had conversations with each council member individually,

02:53:02.733 --> 02:53:06.444
and I believe there probably is a propensity toward that. So in

02:53:06.944 --> 02:53:09.094
the interest of time, I'm going to make a motion if you'll allow it.

02:53:09.576 --> 02:53:13.415
I'm okay with it. Mayor, I move that the city council, uh,

02:53:13.961 --> 02:53:18.202
let me get this right, adopt a resolution repealing

02:53:18.250 --> 02:53:22.619
a property tax increase above the certified rate for fiscal year 2026-2027.

02:53:23.149 --> 02:53:26.826
Second. Okay, we have a motion by Council Member Wright

02:53:27.326 --> 02:53:30.439
and a second by Council Member Clark, and we will start

02:53:30.939 --> 02:53:34.212
the vote with Council Member Whiting. Yes. Council Member Wood. No.

02:53:34.999 --> 02:53:38.820
Uh, Council Member Hughes. Yes. Council Member

02:53:38.852 --> 02:53:42.160
Clark. Yes. Council Member Wright. Yes. Okay,

02:53:42.722 --> 02:53:46.078
that passes 4-1, and, uh, we'll move on to

02:53:46.238 --> 02:53:50.864
item 13B,

02:53:50.945 --> 02:53:54.583
uh, same thing. Uh, I think this is where the conversation

02:53:55.083 --> 02:53:58.933
is going to happen. So anybody that wants to speak, uh, Councilmember Wood,

02:53:58.949 --> 02:54:04.010
I'm happy if you want to start off with— First

02:54:04.510 --> 02:54:06.535
of all, let me say, just because I disagree with that, that doesn't mean I'm

02:54:06.567 --> 02:54:08.821
not going to be in the conversation for the rest of it. That's why I

02:54:09.321 --> 02:54:13.395
wanted to start. Um, when in talking with Councilmember

02:54:13.895 --> 02:54:17.513
Hewish, when we were talking about the code So, just to review what that is,

02:54:17.930 --> 02:54:21.376
we're talking about all of the property tax being applied to the

02:54:21.876 --> 02:54:25.687
public safety, having a separate fund that's specific and has

02:54:26.023 --> 02:54:28.620
parameters where it cannot be spent for anything else.

02:54:29.309 --> 02:54:32.578
Um, that, that ordinance is in place. And then

02:54:32.675 --> 02:54:36.136
there's some parameters of 95% of the contract,

02:54:36.441 --> 02:54:40.560
85% of the contract, and 75%. So, my request

02:54:40.608 --> 02:54:43.284
was, is I asked, if we're going to do that, then we probably ought to

02:54:43.333 --> 02:54:46.474
put our money where our mouth is and say, What does that actually

02:54:46.538 --> 02:54:50.626
look like to the residents? So I'm

02:54:50.642 --> 02:54:52.854
the truth teller, so I'll be the one to tell you what the truth is.

02:54:52.950 --> 02:54:57.919
The truth is that we are going to be canceling the tax relationship

02:54:58.419 --> 02:55:02.150
with UFSA, which is our fire services. The reasoning

02:55:02.199 --> 02:55:05.517
behind that is that we are paying more than we are getting back out of

02:55:05.549 --> 02:55:08.803
that contract. And so, as a result of that,

02:55:09.059 --> 02:55:12.617
so you're paying right now about 0.17 tax

02:55:12.922 --> 02:55:17.033
To that entity, which means that there's going to be a UFA contract

02:55:17.258 --> 02:55:19.971
next year that we're going to have to look at, and there will be a

02:55:20.471 --> 02:55:24.307
cost associated with that. So you need to know what that actually looks

02:55:24.807 --> 02:55:28.305
like. So if we were to do a direct transfer, $0.17 million,

02:55:29.124 --> 02:55:32.784
and then on top of whatever we make the decision tonight, that needs to fall

02:55:32.897 --> 02:55:36.526
within what the parameters are for that code. So it needs to be at least

02:55:37.026 --> 02:55:41.087
75%. of what that total contract is for both our

02:55:41.587 --> 02:55:43.373
sheriff's contract and our fire contract.

02:55:45.338 --> 02:55:47.447
I want to say that to you, so if you don't understand when you come

02:55:47.947 --> 02:55:52.035
up to, to give us feedback, please say that to us. That's how I'm

02:55:52.535 --> 02:55:55.027
going to be evaluating this, because if we don't believe that, then why do the

02:55:55.527 --> 02:55:58.889
code? And that's the reality of it. Why put a code that we're

02:55:59.389 --> 02:56:03.442
not going to follow? So the reason I voted no is because in

02:56:03.540 --> 02:56:07.048
order for us to accomplish just above the threshold of 75%,

02:56:07.436 --> 02:56:08.907
we need to be at least 0.149,

02:56:11.172 --> 02:56:13.542
which is 0.15 where we were.

02:56:17.010 --> 02:56:20.962
On top of that, you'll have the 0.17, even though that won't be taxed directly

02:56:20.994 --> 02:56:23.829
to your property. We'll have a contract that will equal that.

02:56:27.560 --> 02:56:30.924
Councilmember Hughes, wasn't there a different number you had calculated on that, or is that

02:56:31.039 --> 02:56:34.888
what— are you coming up with the same number? So the, the UFSA

02:56:35.388 --> 02:56:39.385
contract, and I've got my, my property tax statement

02:56:39.885 --> 02:56:43.250
here carried around with me these days. Kind of weird,

02:56:43.330 --> 02:56:47.435
but the current rate is $0.001656.

02:56:48.440 --> 02:56:49.596
That's what we pay. Yeah,

02:56:49.821 --> 02:56:52.809
$0.001656.

02:56:53.597 --> 02:56:57.372
It's roughly the same contract as what we're considering with the

02:56:57.872 --> 02:57:02.134
sheriff's office. From a cost perspective. So the 1.7 rate

02:57:02.634 --> 02:57:06.100
for— or the 1.656 rate for the fire is

02:57:06.229 --> 02:57:09.729
pretty close to the 1.7. Now, that would be fully funded.

02:57:09.825 --> 02:57:13.486
And what Councilmember Rich— or either way,

02:57:13.535 --> 02:57:17.468
Councilmember Wood is saying is the UFSA

02:57:17.968 --> 02:57:23.008
today is 100% funded at the 0.00156

02:57:23.409 --> 02:57:26.379
rate. Where I maybe differ with this, I,

02:57:26.619 --> 02:57:31.225
I'm maybe disagreeing with my own code year

02:57:31.273 --> 02:57:35.109
1, but I think we can work into it year 2.

02:57:35.847 --> 02:57:39.940
This volatility in the tax rate is not a

02:57:40.440 --> 02:57:43.952
fault of residents, and I feel like we're kind of asking residents to absorb

02:57:44.452 --> 02:57:48.333
that in 1 year. For some people it's fine, but there

02:57:48.510 --> 02:57:52.455
are many, it's evident that that they can absorb it this

02:57:52.955 --> 02:57:56.174
year. It's going to be challenging for them. So what I did is I ran

02:57:56.607 --> 02:58:00.759
a— to answer Councilmember Whiting's comment— is

02:58:00.951 --> 02:58:04.959
I ran a blended rate. This would be starting on January 1st of next

02:58:05.459 --> 02:58:09.239
year when UFA becomes part of— or UFA,

02:58:09.687 --> 02:58:13.102
when we are negotiating our own contract— to

02:58:13.438 --> 02:58:16.757
come out to a 76% coverage ratio

02:58:17.257 --> 02:58:20.523
for both Sheriff and for fire, that means our

02:58:21.023 --> 02:58:26.870
sheriff contract, the rate would need to be 0.0009

02:58:27.711 --> 02:58:31.467
to achieve a 76% coverage ratio for both fire

02:58:31.823 --> 02:58:37.426
and for sheriff. And so that that's the math that

02:58:37.539 --> 02:58:41.403
that would pass or or meet muster next

02:58:41.903 --> 02:58:44.546
year, and I think we can work into it. Uh, gradually.

02:58:45.906 --> 02:58:48.156
Does that, does that answer your question, Council Member Whiting?

02:58:54.586 --> 02:58:55.729
There's no other comments.

02:58:59.136 --> 02:59:02.871
Go ahead, make the motion. Wait, are we

02:59:03.371 --> 02:59:06.524
gonna— what, is there gonna be public comment for this? No, that's why I'm asking.

02:59:06.573 --> 02:59:09.758
I've— there is public comment still, still here, so Yeah, did you have

02:59:10.258 --> 02:59:13.404
a comment? Yeah, I think briefly, I think, I think we need to acknowledge that

02:59:13.904 --> 02:59:16.938
Eagle Mountain City has a slightly different

02:59:17.438 --> 02:59:21.467
situation this week than a handful of days ago, in that the Tyson plant

02:59:21.820 --> 02:59:26.526
announced a closure that was not part of any of the consideration

02:59:26.638 --> 02:59:30.381
when we first met. And so I, I think the public, if we didn't

02:59:30.397 --> 02:59:32.677
acknowledge it, I think the public would come up and talk about that as well.

02:59:32.742 --> 02:59:36.740
And I think in terms of, in terms of the vote tonight

02:59:36.821 --> 02:59:40.225
and considering a repeal, the— when I, when I personally heard of the,

02:59:40.369 --> 02:59:43.789
the Tyson closure, my first immediate response is

02:59:43.886 --> 02:59:47.595
I sent a message to our economic development director. I said, how many Eagle Mountain

02:59:48.095 --> 02:59:51.320
families specifically are affected? Because we know not all that work at the plant are

02:59:51.769 --> 02:59:55.527
from Eagle Mountain. Some come from other locations. It turns out to be about half,

02:59:55.767 --> 02:59:59.589
which is a significant number. That prompted in my own mind

03:00:00.022 --> 03:00:04.301
a need to to, to measure what we're doing here and,

03:00:04.479 --> 03:00:06.965
uh, and, and to balance out what we're, what we're working on.

03:00:12.624 --> 03:00:15.517
If, if there's no other comments, I can open it up for the public.

03:00:15.742 --> 03:00:19.422
Um, really quick, Mayor, sorry, I just really

03:00:19.455 --> 03:00:23.601
want to make sure our residents understand. And we talked about

03:00:24.054 --> 03:00:27.419
switching out of UFSA. We'll still have the UFA services.

03:00:28.718 --> 03:00:31.945
Um, we just won't be being taxed by them. We're going to

03:00:32.445 --> 03:00:36.233
shift that burden off of that. So we have more control over it. And I

03:00:36.345 --> 03:00:39.492
think there were a lot of numbers thrown out, and I just want to make

03:00:39.992 --> 03:00:43.426
sure everybody understands that at the very least,

03:00:43.811 --> 03:00:47.151
it's going to be that contract price or

03:00:47.681 --> 03:00:50.973
less, because we now, as a city, will get

03:00:51.473 --> 03:00:54.350
to help set what our level of service is. So I don't want everyone to

03:00:54.850 --> 03:00:58.730
be like, oh my gosh, it's gonna be 12,000% increase. It's not.

03:00:59.279 --> 03:01:02.350
What happens is you won't have to pay taxes to UFSA,

03:01:03.206 --> 03:01:07.038
and instead we'll be paying through our contract here.

03:01:07.795 --> 03:01:11.659
But we want you guys to not get scared about

03:01:12.159 --> 03:01:14.683
it because we'll walk through it all together. Thank you.

03:01:14.748 --> 03:01:18.718
Thank you.

03:01:19.056 --> 03:01:20.692
Okay, and just another comment as well.

03:01:22.800 --> 03:01:26.696
The initial request for the money and the

03:01:27.196 --> 03:01:30.382
taxation is backed up by a

03:01:30.431 --> 03:01:32.774
large number of needs that are— that exist here in the city.

03:01:34.143 --> 03:01:37.735
And so I— some people said, well, it was just a head fake. No,

03:01:37.767 --> 03:01:41.070
that's not. We're putting out there saying, look, there's a monetary need in the city.

03:01:42.156 --> 03:01:46.111
That began a discussion, and we're grateful for that discussion

03:01:46.144 --> 03:01:48.722
that happened. Part of, part of my,

03:01:50.320 --> 03:01:53.076
you know, being very open to reconsider this is,

03:01:54.389 --> 03:01:57.161
is something that you alluded to earlier, Mayor, and that you've had some,

03:01:57.620 --> 03:02:01.042
some conversations with some of our business partners in our

03:02:01.542 --> 03:02:04.738
city. And, and part of my willingness to,

03:02:04.867 --> 03:02:09.278
to, to adjust the rate down further right now is

03:02:09.310 --> 03:02:12.664
because of hopes that I have that we can have some positive outcomes

03:02:12.680 --> 03:02:15.775
with those discussions. And that,

03:02:16.656 --> 03:02:19.750
because I want to assure there, there are a number of residents that have,

03:02:19.942 --> 03:02:23.805
have messaged us saying, thank you for this tax increase, because they

03:02:24.305 --> 03:02:27.075
know what it means to invest in, in what those dollars will mean for the

03:02:27.575 --> 03:02:31.338
city. And so, to those residents, I also want to acknowledge that if there's

03:02:31.838 --> 03:02:35.698
a reduction in rate, it's not because we are, we are deciding

03:02:35.794 --> 03:02:38.903
to, to take off the gas from the growth that,

03:02:39.641 --> 03:02:42.109
from the, from the infrastructure dollars that this city needs.

03:02:42.607 --> 03:02:45.692
To take off the gas from so many improvements that the city

03:02:46.192 --> 03:02:49.759
needs. It just means that we, we feel that we've got avenues that

03:02:50.259 --> 03:02:50.771
could potentially help with that.

03:02:53.660 --> 03:02:56.134
And one of those is, uh, I spent some time with some of our federal

03:02:56.150 --> 03:02:59.675
partners, as mentioned, Mike Kennedy. And if you think I didn't ask him for every

03:02:59.708 --> 03:03:02.910
penny I could get back out of him that we already gave him, meaning the

03:03:03.410 --> 03:03:07.588
federal government, you need to come talk to me because we are going

03:03:07.620 --> 03:03:10.217
to advocate for those dollars. So, um,

03:03:12.343 --> 03:03:16.173
I think, I think it's fair to say I want to hear

03:03:16.673 --> 03:03:19.808
from the public, and I hope that you have enough information on this.

03:03:20.695 --> 03:03:24.343
Um, and I'm happy to answer some questions as we

03:03:24.843 --> 03:03:27.926
go along after we finish the public comment as well. I'll keep notes, and I'm

03:03:27.975 --> 03:03:31.363
happy to address those as we all can. So with that, we will

03:03:31.461 --> 03:03:34.708
reopen the public comment at 8:34. All right.

03:03:36.889 --> 03:03:40.741
And, uh, and ask Lacey

03:03:41.482 --> 03:03:43.981
if— and again, if your name is called and you, and you feel like,

03:03:43.997 --> 03:03:47.819
you know what, I, I feel good about where we're headed, just say

03:03:48.497 --> 03:03:51.547
we're good so we can keep going. If you want to speak, speak, or come

03:03:51.579 --> 03:03:54.968
voice your, your opinion. I'm happy with that. I just know that you didn't know

03:03:55.371 --> 03:03:59.370
the conversation yet. Um, this— sorry,

03:03:59.564 --> 03:04:02.999
this first batch is individuals who wrote, um, topic item 13.

03:04:03.629 --> 03:04:07.145
So, I'm not sure what's regarding. So, Anthony Wood.

03:04:14.379 --> 03:04:17.409
All right, so I had a whole comment written out.

03:04:18.344 --> 03:04:20.568
My phone ended up dying, so I'm going to wing it.

03:04:22.894 --> 03:04:25.556
Um, I've talked to a lot of people in Eagle Mountain. I've talked to a

03:04:26.056 --> 03:04:29.784
lot of you guys here. Um, I'm hearing a lot of people talking about needs

03:04:30.284 --> 03:04:33.539
and Realistically,

03:04:33.876 --> 03:04:37.119
I'm only hearing 2 real common needs

03:04:37.619 --> 03:04:41.005
across a lot of the councilmen and other, other members in Eagle Mountain.

03:04:41.744 --> 03:04:45.373
Um, but where I want to start first is that I'm not a supporter

03:04:45.873 --> 03:04:49.194
of property tax, like, internally. You know, I just also logically understand

03:04:49.612 --> 03:04:53.369
that I don't live in a society that affords me to have no property taxes.

03:04:53.722 --> 03:04:56.837
Just on principle, I don't support it. All that

03:04:57.337 --> 03:05:00.597
being said, I do understand that there may be a need for an increase.

03:05:00.870 --> 03:05:04.613
I think your guys' first, first ask was too much. I feel like your guys'

03:05:05.143 --> 03:05:08.221
2nd number you landed on with 183 was still a bit

03:05:08.269 --> 03:05:11.899
high coming out at the 0015 mark.

03:05:13.843 --> 03:05:17.349
Looking at the common need that a lot of councilmen have

03:05:18.266 --> 03:05:21.224
discussed for officers and staff.

03:05:22.707 --> 03:05:26.041
Looking at those 2 needs, those 2 asks there,

03:05:27.790 --> 03:05:31.155
I was looking at a number of about 0.001054.

03:05:31.831 --> 03:05:34.585
The reason why I was coming out to that number is that it equates to

03:05:35.085 --> 03:05:38.342
covering the basic staff needs that were being asked and those

03:05:38.439 --> 03:05:42.094
officers. I feel like the first

03:05:42.594 --> 03:05:46.186
request of 220 was a reaction to the state's cap legislation.

03:05:48.132 --> 03:05:51.545
And I feel like it was acted on quickly, and then it was

03:05:51.657 --> 03:05:55.134
reduced down. You know, it wasn't reduced down far enough.

03:05:55.967 --> 03:06:00.133
Um, I really feel that we can get

03:06:00.633 --> 03:06:04.139
by with those 2 first needs first and read budget, come back

03:06:04.639 --> 03:06:07.119
to the table in the future and find out if there's more that's needed.

03:06:07.200 --> 03:06:10.741
We're going to have a lot of funds coming in, apparently, from what you guys

03:06:11.241 --> 03:06:15.067
are saying. Now, I know that there were other needs that some of the councilmen

03:06:15.099 --> 03:06:18.517
have Members have stated, and those seem to be

03:06:19.017 --> 03:06:22.519
a little bit more on an individual basis. We were talking about roads.

03:06:24.140 --> 03:06:27.521
I may be misunderstanding, but I thought that was covered by the transportation

03:06:27.537 --> 03:06:30.581
fund and the gas taxes. I may— we

03:06:31.081 --> 03:06:35.194
may not have enough. I don't know. I haven't researched that much yet. But with

03:06:35.694 --> 03:06:38.106
all that being said, that we have things that you guys are looking at that

03:06:38.606 --> 03:06:41.940
can wait. And we can budget those, we can plan those. I'm not

03:06:42.440 --> 03:06:46.415
saying wait. 5 years, 10 years, or whatever. Just take it year by year

03:06:46.768 --> 03:06:49.882
by year, and let's adjust as needed. If we do have funds

03:06:49.898 --> 03:06:53.766
coming in, then we can adjust to that. I don't think we should be reliant

03:06:53.911 --> 03:06:57.939
on any external entity to the city, so I do believe we should have some

03:06:58.439 --> 03:07:02.177
property taxes. I would hate to see the data centers leave and leave us in

03:07:02.677 --> 03:07:05.820
a hole where we need more money. I, I don't like the data centers.

03:07:05.884 --> 03:07:09.528
Let me get that out there as well. But consider a lower number that

03:07:09.576 --> 03:07:11.149
might be a little bit more realistic, please.

03:07:14.923 --> 03:07:15.504
Wade S.

03:07:20.973 --> 03:07:24.037
I don't see Wade. Ashley Erkschein.

03:07:25.730 --> 03:07:26.827
Feel free to correct me if I'm wrong.

03:07:29.988 --> 03:07:33.968
All right. So I'm

03:07:34.468 --> 03:07:36.865
not a public speaker, and I really hate that I have to be here tonight.

03:07:37.192 --> 03:07:41.076
Just say no. But I would like to just make sure I

03:07:41.205 --> 03:07:44.255
formally oppose any tax increase at this time on

03:07:44.755 --> 03:07:48.156
Eagle Mountain citizens. I believe that demanding a financial burden—

03:07:49.087 --> 03:07:52.361
a permanent, sorry, financial burden on taxpayers at

03:07:52.861 --> 03:07:57.065
a time when your constituents are already strained by the economy is completely

03:07:57.161 --> 03:08:01.062
irresponsible and unnecessary. Your constituents

03:08:01.431 --> 03:08:04.529
are people— are the people who actually built this city.

03:08:05.543 --> 03:08:09.265
The people who voted for you and trusted you to look

03:08:09.765 --> 03:08:13.028
out for their best interests. You made claims

03:08:13.044 --> 03:08:16.731
that we'll see revenue from data centers, as Anthony mentioned a moment ago,

03:08:17.703 --> 03:08:21.002
within the next year. So do we really need

03:08:21.502 --> 03:08:23.493
a tax increase now, a permanent tax increase?

03:08:25.190 --> 03:08:28.783
Historically, you know, there was a, there was a thought.

03:08:29.285 --> 03:08:32.101
I think it was 1913 when income taxes started.

03:08:32.166 --> 03:08:36.119
Wasn't that supposed to be temporary too? If we know we

03:08:36.619 --> 03:08:40.320
have revenue coming and we know that we

03:08:40.820 --> 03:08:44.345
can get by for another year, right, evaluate, assess, be careful,

03:08:44.864 --> 03:08:48.335
be thoughtful about permanent decisions, we should

03:08:48.835 --> 03:08:52.081
do so. If these needs are

03:08:52.581 --> 03:08:56.315
so necessary and we need them right now, then those

03:08:56.589 --> 03:08:59.712
of you who served this city for the past 2 to

03:08:59.793 --> 03:09:02.928
8 years Should have planned and budgeted these things

03:09:02.960 --> 03:09:06.091
sooner. For example, I would like

03:09:06.591 --> 03:09:10.507
to know why the city spent $7.3 million on land for a civic

03:09:11.007 --> 03:09:13.670
center, aka new city hall, just last year.

03:09:15.147 --> 03:09:18.824
Without evaluating the need for public safety, wastewater plant

03:09:19.242 --> 03:09:22.999
raises for its employees, or even additional employees

03:09:23.352 --> 03:09:26.786
to maintain what the city already has. Why are we buying

03:09:26.835 --> 03:09:30.298
more land if we cannot maintain what we already have?

03:09:34.647 --> 03:09:37.498
Sorry, I lost my spot. There has to be a point where we look at

03:09:37.998 --> 03:09:41.678
the budget and see what can be reduced and make sure that these

03:09:41.776 --> 03:09:45.213
things are planned and prioritized at the appropriate time.

03:09:46.551 --> 03:09:48.855
And frankly, true leadership requires integrity,

03:09:49.790 --> 03:09:53.190
requires the integrity to take accountability for those who, who you

03:09:53.256 --> 03:09:56.703
bear responsibility for. excuses and walks around the truth,

03:09:57.168 --> 03:09:59.543
moving money around, coming up with new funds,

03:10:00.120 --> 03:10:04.195
shifting stuff here, there. That doesn't— that displays

03:10:04.628 --> 03:10:07.885
an inability to drive results. And that's something

03:10:08.078 --> 03:10:11.126
I don't think this city can afford. Ultimately,

03:10:11.286 --> 03:10:14.382
if you guys think about it, I just want you to think about one thing.

03:10:15.040 --> 03:10:18.971
Um, and I'm just going to go to the end here, but I would like

03:10:19.471 --> 03:10:23.282
you to consider the fact that Your choices— you guys are all on a governing

03:10:23.395 --> 03:10:27.011
body in the United States of America, right? And so your choices have a

03:10:27.511 --> 03:10:31.379
direct impact on businesses. Businesses offset their costs

03:10:31.879 --> 03:10:35.787
onto consumers. So you are directly affecting the bigger problem in the United

03:10:36.287 --> 03:10:39.289
States of America, which is inflation. Let's not do that.

03:10:39.484 --> 03:10:43.681
Thanks. Your time is up. Thank you. Jen Hackett.

03:10:51.725 --> 03:10:55.305
My name is Jen Hackett. Um, I understand our city has grown

03:10:55.354 --> 03:10:58.806
tremendously and we haven't raised property taxes in a long time,

03:10:59.512 --> 03:11:03.093
and that some of the decisions that have brought us here were made by past

03:11:03.125 --> 03:11:06.401
leadership. But I'm asking you tonight to really consider how much

03:11:06.433 --> 03:11:10.383
we actually need this right now and to be completely transparent with residents

03:11:10.883 --> 03:11:14.250
about what we're paying for. This letter that we received says we hear

03:11:14.298 --> 03:11:17.796
you and that every dollar of this increase will go directly toward public safety.

03:11:18.453 --> 03:11:22.208
Technically, that's true. When I read it, the first 2 paragraphs

03:11:22.240 --> 03:11:25.897
already, I was upset with it. It's misleading

03:11:26.154 --> 03:11:30.004
at best and manipulative at its worst. The average resident

03:11:30.504 --> 03:11:33.486
reading this letter is going to believe this tax increase is needed to pay for

03:11:33.502 --> 03:11:37.609
new public safety expenses. But that's not the whole story. We need

03:11:37.625 --> 03:11:41.090
1. $1.5 million for additional deputies. The rest of the sheriff's

03:11:41.590 --> 03:11:45.727
contract is already paid for, and moving that existing expense to property taxes

03:11:45.743 --> 03:11:48.037
is going to free up millions of dollars for other things.

03:11:48.872 --> 03:11:51.888
Just tell us that. Tell us where that money is going.

03:11:52.465 --> 03:11:56.059
For example, if it was going to hire groundskeepers to maintain raw spaces

03:11:56.091 --> 03:11:59.605
behind our communities, to clear tumbleweeds and dead grass,

03:11:59.621 --> 03:12:03.199
and to protect our homes from fire, then say that and tell us what

03:12:03.215 --> 03:12:06.728
that costs. Fund what you say you're going to fund and be accountable for doing

03:12:06.744 --> 03:12:10.485
it. Thank you. We've heard capital projects. That's not specific enough.

03:12:11.079 --> 03:12:14.708
Which projects are they? What do they cost? What needs to happen now and

03:12:15.208 --> 03:12:18.690
what can wait? We keep hearing additional revenue is around the corner.

03:12:19.782 --> 03:12:22.897
So, if we're in dire financial straits and we cannot wait for

03:12:23.397 --> 03:12:26.831
that revenue, tell us we're in dire financial straits. Residents can handle

03:12:27.331 --> 03:12:30.893
tough answers. We're being told it's just a little bit more. It's only $1

03:12:30.990 --> 03:12:35.064
or $2 a day. It's this much. We're giving

03:12:35.096 --> 03:12:38.110
a little to so many more places right now, more for groceries,

03:12:38.206 --> 03:12:41.765
utilities, insurance, and gas. This increase

03:12:42.006 --> 03:12:45.517
is enough for formula for a baby for a few months. It's a year of

03:12:46.017 --> 03:12:48.931
school lunches for a student who doesn't qualify for free lunch.

03:12:49.508 --> 03:12:53.292
It's the fee for an entire cross-country season for a high school student.

03:12:53.757 --> 03:12:57.187
It's school fees for 2 students. It's a couple weeks of groceries

03:12:57.300 --> 03:13:00.878
for a young family. Thank you. It's around 5 tanks of gas to get somebody

03:13:00.910 --> 03:13:04.152
to work. Um, you can believe this tax increase

03:13:04.264 --> 03:13:07.555
is necessary without minimizing what you're asking people to give up.

03:13:08.293 --> 03:13:11.808
Tonight was a poor choice for this meeting. Tomorrow's the first day

03:13:12.308 --> 03:13:15.981
of school for most students in our community. Parents are home getting kids

03:13:16.481 --> 03:13:18.870
in bed right now and ready for school. They may want to be here,

03:13:18.950 --> 03:13:22.128
and you should want them to be here. Mayor Gray,

03:13:23.220 --> 03:13:26.430
I know that you attended the last meeting by Zoom. Excuse me. Residents made the

03:13:26.930 --> 03:13:29.881
effort to show up, sit in that room. They deserve to have you here.

03:13:30.346 --> 03:13:33.914
to look them in the eyes and hear what they had to say. Um,

03:13:33.978 --> 03:13:37.450
I'm not asking for you to never raise our taxes, but I am asking before

03:13:37.950 --> 03:13:41.468
you vote to consider what we need and moving forward to be honest and

03:13:41.968 --> 03:13:45.127
straightforward with your communication and tell us what we're getting for our money.

03:13:45.418 --> 03:13:45.823
Thank you.

03:13:49.786 --> 03:13:50.530
Steve Peretta.

03:14:00.273 --> 03:14:03.308
Good evening. My name is Steve Perretta. Uh,

03:14:03.342 --> 03:14:07.249
thank you for allowing me to talk. Uh, I want

03:14:07.749 --> 03:14:10.497
to echo what the last lady said. I'm glad to see you could all find

03:14:10.997 --> 03:14:14.037
the time to be here today. Uh, there is sarcasm attached to that. I would

03:14:14.216 --> 03:14:17.512
expect that under— uh, unless we're talking

03:14:17.561 --> 03:14:20.874
serious, serious emergencies, I would expect that all 6 of

03:14:21.374 --> 03:14:25.110
you would be here to address our concerns. Transparency comes before

03:14:25.610 --> 03:14:29.429
taxes, not the other way around. You tell us you're not communicating effectively and

03:14:29.445 --> 03:14:32.512
need to do better, but you voted unanimously for 183%,

03:14:32.801 --> 03:14:36.446
and only after the people spoke up did you start talk—

03:14:36.575 --> 03:14:39.625
start talking compromise. That's backwards. That's not the way it's

03:14:40.125 --> 03:14:43.655
supposed to work. I emailed all of you on the 7th, one day after the

03:14:44.155 --> 03:14:46.160
last meeting. 3 of you responded, 50%.

03:14:48.744 --> 03:14:52.696
Council members Huish, Whiting, and Clark, in that order.

03:14:53.940 --> 03:14:57.711
Councilmember Clark's response didn't come till today, 2 weeks after I emailed,

03:14:57.744 --> 03:15:00.767
or almost 2 weeks after I emailed you. My wife and I had a long

03:15:00.864 --> 03:15:04.147
discussion with Councilman— Councilmember

03:15:04.502 --> 03:15:06.928
Huish, and I appreciate that. Thank you.

03:15:08.464 --> 03:15:11.612
Uh, but I still haven't seen the transparency we're asking for. Why are we trying

03:15:11.645 --> 03:15:14.931
to fund an entire public safety need solely out of

03:15:14.947 --> 03:15:17.671
property tax. That's not the way it's been done in the past. Why are we

03:15:18.171 --> 03:15:20.972
trying to do that in the future? Mayor Gray, you told my wife and I

03:15:21.472 --> 03:15:24.866
directly before you were the mayor that there would be data center growth

03:15:24.882 --> 03:15:28.199
that would equal $50 a month for each household in

03:15:28.247 --> 03:15:31.308
Eagle Mountain. It was, it was not on the record.

03:15:32.173 --> 03:15:35.554
Uh, it was after a meeting after my

03:15:36.054 --> 03:15:39.496
wife and I had both voiced our displeasure. Simple math says $50 a month

03:15:39.996 --> 03:15:43.430
equals $600 a year. Thank you. But now you're asking for a $300 a year

03:15:43.575 --> 03:15:46.987
increase. That's a $900 swing from a

03:15:47.487 --> 03:15:50.551
decrease of $600 a month to an increase of $900 a month. This is not

03:15:51.051 --> 03:15:54.530
difficult math. Wrong direction from what we

03:15:54.546 --> 03:15:58.183
were told to expect. You said tonight you support QTS,

03:15:58.199 --> 03:16:01.901
but you're still asking us for a tax increase before, before giving us the transparency

03:16:02.401 --> 03:16:05.860
that we've asked for. You want our support? Support what

03:16:05.893 --> 03:16:09.529
we're asking for and we'll support you. Thank you. I submitted a GRAMA

03:16:10.029 --> 03:16:13.603
request after the last meeting to understand how the 183% figure

03:16:13.956 --> 03:16:17.564
was actually calculated. The city denied my fee

03:16:18.064 --> 03:16:21.493
waiver and is now requiring a $100 deposit before they

03:16:21.589 --> 03:16:25.406
even begin processing a request for records that should already be

03:16:25.906 --> 03:16:29.239
public. So, from where I sit, the city is asking—

03:16:29.287 --> 03:16:33.265
excuse me, the city is making transparency cost

03:16:33.765 --> 03:16:36.394
money. Thank you. I expect each of you to decide how you're voting tonight.

03:16:39.502 --> 03:16:43.165
Uh, after hearing tonight's comments, uh, you each— I'll be

03:16:43.665 --> 03:16:48.084
quick here. This council represents 0.0078%

03:16:48.584 --> 03:16:52.418
of our population. That means each of you represents about 12,782

03:16:52.450 --> 03:16:55.871
residents each. So, to your point, Councilmember Gray,

03:16:56.469 --> 03:16:59.831
uh, yes, it's a heavy burden, and I expect you to vote accordingly.

03:16:59.879 --> 03:17:04.069
Thank you. according to what your constituents would want you to do. Your time

03:17:04.569 --> 03:17:07.695
is up. Thank you. Alex Washburn.

03:17:16.279 --> 03:17:19.338
Can come back if he's— Natalie Deschamons.

03:17:26.399 --> 03:17:30.049
Hi there. I'm Natalie Deschamont. I am one of

03:17:30.549 --> 03:17:34.964
the people who originally co-sponsored the referendum. It has been a

03:17:35.012 --> 03:17:38.583
long week of civic duty, and so I got a little bit of taste of

03:17:39.083 --> 03:17:40.878
what you guys do, and I have no interest in doing it. I've learned that

03:17:40.926 --> 03:17:44.591
this week. While I don't regret what

03:17:45.205 --> 03:17:48.598
we submitted, I'm very proud of being part of a referendum and

03:17:48.614 --> 03:17:52.158
standing up for the people of the community. I want

03:17:52.658 --> 03:17:56.044
to make note that multiple members of the council and Mayor Gray himself

03:17:56.172 --> 03:18:00.282
took the time to sit with us and talk with us and respond to the

03:18:00.782 --> 03:18:03.253
things that my husband and I had to say and questions that we had.

03:18:03.719 --> 03:18:07.042
Um, I understand the need for a tax increase.

03:18:07.267 --> 03:18:10.719
I think that the one that was originally passed obviously was too high. I think

03:18:11.219 --> 03:18:14.300
we all recognize that. Um, I don't know what the right number is.

03:18:14.814 --> 03:18:18.524
I don't do numbers. I'm a— I'm a teacher, so I'm not

03:18:18.572 --> 03:18:21.175
a— I'm not a number person, right? I'm a people person in that sense.

03:18:21.239 --> 03:18:24.582
But I don't know the right number, but I recognize

03:18:24.678 --> 03:18:28.513
the need for an increase. And I appreciate that while

03:18:28.562 --> 03:18:31.583
it may have been because your backs were against the wall from public outcry,

03:18:31.631 --> 03:18:34.539
that you guys did take the time to sit and reflect and reach out to

03:18:35.039 --> 03:18:38.322
us, at least us personally. And that really

03:18:38.338 --> 03:18:41.585
is my public comment. So, Mayor Gray, I appreciate the time we took last week.

03:18:42.860 --> 03:18:46.338
Councilmember Hewish, I appreciate you responding to my husband and having a thoughtful conversation with

03:18:46.354 --> 03:18:49.671
him. And I hope that whatever the resolution

03:18:50.171 --> 03:18:53.970
comes to be today, I hope that we all can agree that conversations

03:18:54.470 --> 03:18:57.764
have been had and people have been heard on both sides. So that is my

03:18:58.264 --> 03:18:58.458
comment. Thank you, guys.

03:19:01.690 --> 03:19:02.639
Laura Albright.

03:19:15.544 --> 03:19:18.913
This is new for me. I'm just going to read the

03:19:19.413 --> 03:19:23.565
last sentence of what I have written down. Mayor Gray

03:19:23.725 --> 03:19:27.046
and City Council, my— and obviously my name

03:19:27.546 --> 03:19:31.024
is Laura Albrecht. Um, I'm just asking, and this

03:19:31.524 --> 03:19:34.137
was after my, my whole page, um,

03:19:34.393 --> 03:19:38.227
isn't there just one more way to work this out rather

03:19:38.243 --> 03:19:42.123
than causing much distress to the citizens

03:19:42.268 --> 03:19:45.485
of this great city. And I want

03:19:45.985 --> 03:19:49.297
to thank you for what I have heard, for, for what all of it I

03:19:49.345 --> 03:19:52.495
can understand. I can't understand all of it, but, um,

03:19:53.925 --> 03:19:56.465
I can tell that you've put your heads together and,

03:19:57.204 --> 03:20:00.806
and there's been, uh, a good groupthink.

03:20:01.667 --> 03:20:05.386
And, and I hope that we can move forward and not have to worry

03:20:05.435 --> 03:20:08.929
about This— I'm sure that next time it comes

03:20:09.026 --> 03:20:12.566
up, and like this last little lady said, I realize

03:20:13.002 --> 03:20:16.478
we've got to have taxes to live. That's just all there is to it.

03:20:16.785 --> 03:20:19.956
But in the meantime, I hope we can do it differently than we did

03:20:20.456 --> 03:20:21.833
this last time. Thank you.

03:20:25.943 --> 03:20:26.639
Melissa Bradley.

03:20:34.324 --> 03:20:37.923
Tonight's not a good night to be here because of school starting tomorrow,

03:20:38.164 --> 03:20:41.475
um, and I was in Provo all week— or all day today helping my

03:20:41.539 --> 03:20:45.154
25-year-old daughter pack so she could move back home with

03:20:45.654 --> 03:20:48.963
us on Saturday. I know each of you have rejected the idea

03:20:49.091 --> 03:20:52.723
that, um, your tax increase will affect

03:20:53.223 --> 03:20:56.483
rent for our children, but I want you all to know and warn you that

03:20:56.983 --> 03:21:00.690
it will Raise rent, and landlords will pass that tax increase on

03:21:00.723 --> 03:21:04.122
to our children. I'm here tonight

03:21:04.622 --> 03:21:08.289
because I believe we need honesty about the property tax increase and to stop blaming

03:21:08.321 --> 03:21:09.985
the past decisions,

03:21:11.616 --> 03:21:14.768
um, that are being made today. We keep hearing that

03:21:14.849 --> 03:21:18.875
Eagle Mountain has to raise property taxes by 183% because

03:21:19.214 --> 03:21:22.946
previous councils made mistakes, that they were cheap.

03:21:24.293 --> 03:21:28.399
They weren't cheap. They were intelligent. That is simply not

03:21:28.463 --> 03:21:31.719
the whole story. Past mayors and councils built this city.

03:21:32.152 --> 03:21:35.006
They faced enormous challenges, lawsuits,

03:21:35.760 --> 03:21:38.534
rapid growth, and limited resources.

03:21:39.208 --> 03:21:43.057
They chose to live within the revenue that they had rather

03:21:43.557 --> 03:21:46.746
than continually asking taxpayers for more.

03:21:47.772 --> 03:21:50.403
It's easy to spend more money. When you have more money.

03:21:51.640 --> 03:21:54.787
What is hard is being fiscally responsible.

03:21:55.654 --> 03:21:59.716
What is hard is saying we can't do everything

03:21:59.813 --> 03:22:03.618
right now. Let's prioritize. Let's grow carefully. Let's make

03:22:04.118 --> 03:22:07.375
sure every dollar is spent wisely before we take another dollar from our

03:22:07.875 --> 03:22:11.373
residents. That's leadership. And I want

03:22:11.873 --> 03:22:15.854
to address the Gettysburg analogy. Councilman Whiting, Taxpayers are not the

03:22:15.871 --> 03:22:20.645
enemy. We are not the Confederates at

03:22:21.145 --> 03:22:24.324
Round Top. We are your constituents. We elected

03:22:24.824 --> 03:22:28.325
you. We pay the taxes. We pay our taxes. We have the

03:22:28.825 --> 03:22:32.440
right to tell you where we believe our money should and should not be spent.

03:22:33.020 --> 03:22:36.102
We're not declaring war on you. We are simply

03:22:36.602 --> 03:22:40.479
saying no to a tax increase. If anything,

03:22:40.997 --> 03:22:43.814
this is the Boston Tea Party, and we have enough. We've had enough.

03:22:44.332 --> 03:22:47.698
And please look at the, at the people this affects.

03:22:47.779 --> 03:22:51.580
Our seniors came before you all, and they told

03:22:52.080 --> 03:22:55.376
you they are retired on fixed incomes. They do not get to vote

03:22:55.876 --> 03:22:59.545
themselves a raise when property taxes go up. They are the people

03:22:59.739 --> 03:23:02.930
we should be protecting and valuing and not dismissing.

03:23:03.268 --> 03:23:05.621
None of you addressed them last 2 weeks ago.

03:23:06.330 --> 03:23:10.120
None of you. Instead, you voted For

03:23:10.136 --> 03:23:14.255
a tax increase. Mayor, please stop using Facebook to attack

03:23:14.559 --> 03:23:17.797
or misrepresent people that you disagree with. You're the mayor

03:23:17.845 --> 03:23:21.242
of Eagle Mountain. Please take accountability for your

03:23:21.274 --> 03:23:24.624
actions. Please, please stop the attacking

03:23:24.736 --> 03:23:28.615
on Facebook. It's embarrassing. And to the entire

03:23:28.727 --> 03:23:32.269
council, set your egos aside. The plan you came up

03:23:32.769 --> 03:23:36.468
with in St. George is not automatically right because you came up with it.

03:23:36.933 --> 03:23:40.577
Spending more does not automatically. Thank you. Make Eagle Mountain

03:23:40.610 --> 03:23:43.405
better. The hard thing is saying no.

03:23:44.472 --> 03:23:47.946
The hard thing is making difficult choices, and the hard thing is

03:23:48.446 --> 03:23:50.850
admitting— Your time is up. Thank you.

03:23:53.397 --> 03:23:53.981
Joel Buss.

03:24:05.476 --> 03:24:08.705
My name is Joel Buss. Believe it or not, I've never done this before,

03:24:09.026 --> 03:24:12.479
despite who my better half is. Um, but I'd just

03:24:12.979 --> 03:24:15.434
like to make a quick comment about why we're here tonight. We're here because of

03:24:15.515 --> 03:24:18.582
a breakdown in communication, and when communication breaks

03:24:19.082 --> 03:24:22.726
down, you lose trust. It's pretty simple. The pressure this council is feeling

03:24:22.758 --> 03:24:25.441
tonight didn't appear overnight.

03:24:26.517 --> 03:24:30.516
It built because residents, residents asked questions and too often

03:24:30.548 --> 03:24:33.358
walked away without Clear and consistent answers.

03:24:34.643 --> 03:24:38.432
I have no doubt this council believes and knows what

03:24:38.480 --> 03:24:41.612
Eagle Mountain needs. You also have the entire picture.

03:24:42.655 --> 03:24:46.685
We don't. But you as a council can't

03:24:47.185 --> 03:24:50.828
give residents incompetent or conflicting explanations

03:24:50.940 --> 03:24:55.260
and then criticize us for not understanding what hasn't

03:24:55.436 --> 03:24:58.574
been clearly explained. Thank you. You are our leaders,

03:24:58.768 --> 03:25:00.998
and you cannot come across as haphazard.

03:25:03.026 --> 03:25:06.887
If we have 100 problems and they're all priority number 1,

03:25:07.969 --> 03:25:11.207
we need a plan. You need a plan,

03:25:11.809 --> 03:25:13.078
and you need to get on the same page.

03:25:15.322 --> 03:25:19.025
We can't afford to just firehose attack these problems

03:25:19.138 --> 03:25:22.890
and expect a great result. We need

03:25:23.390 --> 03:25:27.214
a strategy. We need to approach them maniacally, deliberately, and with

03:25:27.375 --> 03:25:31.208
absolute clarity. Tell us what's next,

03:25:31.951 --> 03:25:35.486
why it's next, what it costs, and where we're going

03:25:35.519 --> 03:25:39.998
after that. You want us to be involved? Give us opportunities well

03:25:40.047 --> 03:25:43.405
before the due date. That's why we're here tonight.

03:25:45.800 --> 03:25:49.334
Councilmember Wood, I'd like to address you and the comments

03:25:49.834 --> 03:25:54.539
you made about my wife. You called her involvement disappointing

03:25:55.539 --> 03:25:58.037
and suggested it was a publicity stunt.

03:25:59.286 --> 03:26:02.879
I know why she got involved. For 2 weeks straight, I've watched

03:26:03.379 --> 03:26:07.007
her take calls, texts, people show up to my house crying,

03:26:08.747 --> 03:26:13.146
all from residents concerned about a municipal decision

03:26:13.646 --> 03:26:15.418
she has zero authority over.

03:26:17.330 --> 03:26:19.931
Because people are looking for someone who would listen, Rich.

03:26:22.776 --> 03:26:24.925
So she listened. We're all adults.

03:26:26.420 --> 03:26:30.003
Trust us with the information. Accountability means listening

03:26:30.503 --> 03:26:34.077
before public outrage forces it. It shouldn't take 2

03:26:34.141 --> 03:26:37.282
weeks of frustration for residents to finally feel heard.

03:26:38.135 --> 03:26:42.003
Each of you, I know for a fact, could probably list 5 residents

03:26:42.347 --> 03:26:45.542
That are, whether they're a pain in the what, or they're calling you

03:26:45.574 --> 03:26:49.396
left and right, you could include them. You could make them subject matter

03:26:49.492 --> 03:26:52.174
experts that could help you, that could be a voice of the people.

03:26:53.282 --> 03:26:57.055
We all want a safer, stronger Eagle Mountain. The people have

03:26:57.555 --> 03:27:00.587
a voice, and we expect our council to trust us enough to show us the

03:27:01.087 --> 03:27:03.799
plan, explain the why, and let us be a part of how we get there.

03:27:04.280 --> 03:27:04.617
Thank you.

03:27:09.058 --> 03:27:09.687
Adam Bradley.

03:27:14.821 --> 03:27:18.493
So I just want to be clear, you repealed the tax hike?

03:27:18.542 --> 03:27:22.020
Yes, that first vote was repealing the tax

03:27:22.520 --> 03:27:25.305
hike. I'm not that smart and I didn't get it, so I don't know if

03:27:25.805 --> 03:27:28.624
they got it. But the second vote is going to come up with a new

03:27:29.124 --> 03:27:32.010
number, and because it's going to be less than the $183 million, you don't have

03:27:32.510 --> 03:27:34.574
to go through the tax— through the taxation process, am I right?

03:27:36.457 --> 03:27:39.601
No, this is part of that. Okay,

03:27:39.763 --> 03:27:42.488
cool. I'm just trying to understand the process because that's important,

03:27:42.988 --> 03:27:46.350
and you guys live it. We don't. It's not

03:27:46.398 --> 03:27:49.661
always easy to understand, even though some of us might have experience in it.

03:27:50.359 --> 03:27:54.253
It's still out of our purview. So maybe some clarification on

03:27:54.753 --> 03:27:57.587
some of that stuff. So having said that,

03:27:58.424 --> 03:28:02.972
um, I think, I think this whole process kind of Embarrasses

03:28:03.004 --> 03:28:07.444
me. It kind of brings me back to, like, remember 15,

03:28:07.717 --> 03:28:10.859
18 years ago when a lot of us moved here? Eagle Mountain was kind of

03:28:11.359 --> 03:28:14.723
a butt of a lot of jokes, right? Our government was run by just sort

03:28:15.223 --> 03:28:18.153
of like a good old boy club, and they didn't really care, and they did

03:28:18.233 --> 03:28:21.648
weird stuff, and it led to some tragedies, actually,

03:28:21.985 --> 03:28:25.255
right? You remember that? And I felt that, that we've kind of

03:28:25.367 --> 03:28:28.494
become that butt of those jokes again. in the last couple of weeks.

03:28:29.120 --> 03:28:32.616
You see 183 reduced from 220 all

03:28:32.728 --> 03:28:36.754
over the news, all over the place. People don't have context,

03:28:37.300 --> 03:28:41.534
but that's the problem. And so I'm

03:28:41.631 --> 03:28:44.983
also embarrassed that, you know, maybe we don't

03:28:44.999 --> 03:28:48.544
always act great online. It's really easy to be a keyboard warrior, right?

03:28:49.025 --> 03:28:52.971
And so, you know, Melissa, some, you know, those are

03:28:53.471 --> 03:28:55.457
embarrassing comments to hear people saying about you.

03:28:57.320 --> 03:29:01.046
That's not, that's not who we are as a community. That's not who

03:29:01.546 --> 03:29:03.913
we are. So I'm embarrassed by that as well. Um,

03:29:04.950 --> 03:29:09.547
and, and I'm not going to excuse it, but this

03:29:10.047 --> 03:29:13.479
whole process has been bad. I'm glad

03:29:13.979 --> 03:29:18.006
you repealed it. I support that, that you just repealed that. But now our next

03:29:18.070 --> 03:29:20.422
one, what are you going to do? I have no idea what you're going to

03:29:20.922 --> 03:29:23.289
do. And so I support you voting no on the next one. Thank you.

03:29:23.662 --> 03:29:26.454
On 13B as well, and just start over.

03:29:27.433 --> 03:29:30.819
Start over. You all admitted regret, which is maybe the first time

03:29:30.867 --> 03:29:34.397
I've heard that from a lot of you. You all admitted regret in your

03:29:34.897 --> 03:29:38.152
communication, in your transparency.

03:29:39.050 --> 03:29:42.644
Um, I didn't hear anybody say you regret raising taxes,

03:29:42.676 --> 03:29:46.704
because I stand for 0% taxes. I stand

03:29:47.204 --> 03:29:50.940
for— Meaning reducing the taxation on our, on our residents 100%.

03:29:52.047 --> 03:29:55.589
So you might say that's not practical. I say figure it out.

03:29:56.070 --> 03:29:59.243
So taxation is theft. And if you don't believe that,

03:29:59.420 --> 03:30:02.481
then you're the wrong person to represent me. And that's not just a trope.

03:30:02.738 --> 03:30:06.328
Okay. And so the principles I see

03:30:06.828 --> 03:30:10.800
are not, are not there that I agree with. The principles of you

03:30:11.300 --> 03:30:13.990
spend less, you make less, you do what you do with less.

03:30:15.048 --> 03:30:18.510
And sewer, great. Fund the sewer. We got to fund

03:30:19.010 --> 03:30:19.359
the sewer. So. Thank you.

03:30:22.906 --> 03:30:23.681
Gary Fuchs.

03:30:30.254 --> 03:30:33.695
How's it going? My name is Gary Fuchs.

03:30:33.889 --> 03:30:37.268
I lived in Eagle Mountain since 2003, and yes,

03:30:37.381 --> 03:30:40.808
I'm wearing an aloha shirt tonight and shorts to talk about taxes,

03:30:41.002 --> 03:30:44.420
because I figured if my argument is only persuasive when I'm dressed up,

03:30:44.436 --> 03:30:48.239
it probably isn't a very good argument. So I'm going to be comfortable and let

03:30:48.739 --> 03:30:51.819
the numbers speak for themselves. First, thanks for making the hard decisions,

03:30:52.493 --> 03:30:56.282
and I'm sorry for the abuse and threats you and your families have endured.

03:30:56.523 --> 03:30:59.140
It's unacceptable, and we need to be better.

03:30:59.638 --> 03:31:03.748
And shame on those fanning the flames while crying victim. Over the last

03:31:04.248 --> 03:31:08.355
week, I've spent probably more time than I should have with Google and AI digging

03:31:08.452 --> 03:31:12.385
into this tax increase, the budget, the sheriff's contract.

03:31:12.562 --> 03:31:15.896
police staffing in other cities, other Utah cities,

03:31:16.169 --> 03:31:18.750
truth in taxation, and even the data center agreements.

03:31:19.535 --> 03:31:23.030
And after all of that, I support a meaningful

03:31:23.046 --> 03:31:27.294
property tax increase. That doesn't mean that I think the city communicated

03:31:27.794 --> 03:31:31.735
this perfectly. I think 183% became the story while

03:31:32.235 --> 03:31:35.550
100% for public safety was too simple to explain that was

03:31:36.050 --> 03:31:39.862
actually happening. The issue isn't just 7 additional deputies.

03:31:40.295 --> 03:31:44.223
We have around 77,000 residents and one of the lowest law enforcement

03:31:44.723 --> 03:31:47.909
staffing ratios among comparable Utah cities. From my

03:31:48.409 --> 03:31:52.077
research in the last 7 years, calls have risen 223%

03:31:52.638 --> 03:31:55.891
and deputies only about 119%. We also

03:31:56.391 --> 03:32:00.027
have a sheriff's contract that property tax currently does not fully fund.

03:32:00.475 --> 03:32:02.559
Other city revenues are making up that difference.

03:32:03.793 --> 03:32:07.191
Moving more of public safety onto property taxes does 2 things.

03:32:07.768 --> 03:32:12.112
It allows us to add needed deputies, and it frees existing recurring revenue to

03:32:12.612 --> 03:32:15.174
address staffing and other needs in the city that has grown enormously.

03:32:16.183 --> 03:32:19.566
My ask is to share that list with

03:32:20.066 --> 03:32:24.054
the citizens. That's one thing conversations that I've had online is missing is what's

03:32:24.554 --> 03:32:27.933
that list? Do you want us to, to give our input on what's important?

03:32:28.863 --> 03:32:31.940
What's out there, right? And I understand that this

03:32:32.052 --> 03:32:35.355
increase will hurt some families, and that matters, and I don't dismiss

03:32:35.855 --> 03:32:39.442
it. One thought I had while sitting over there is exploring the possibility of

03:32:39.942 --> 03:32:43.359
adopting something Texas did, which is giving breaks to senior citizens over the age of

03:32:43.375 --> 03:32:46.071
65, veterans, and those on disability.

03:32:47.066 --> 03:32:50.421
But I also don't think continuing to postpone the problem is responsible.

03:32:50.758 --> 03:32:53.374
We haven't gone through truth in taxation in 15 years,

03:32:53.887 --> 03:32:57.097
and eventually we have to fund the city we've become, not the city we were

03:32:57.597 --> 03:33:01.094
15 years ago. Whatever rate you settle on tonight, I ask

03:33:01.594 --> 03:33:05.106
you to make— make it actually addresses the problem instead of

03:33:05.122 --> 03:33:08.510
simply choosing the number that creates the least backlash. And will be the

03:33:09.010 --> 03:33:12.190
most politically advantageous. Also, as a side note, I'd rather have more

03:33:12.690 --> 03:33:13.894
data centers than houses. Thank you.

03:33:16.980 --> 03:33:19.862
Garrett Houghter. I'm not sure if I said your last name right.

03:33:20.530 --> 03:33:21.507
Okay, thank you.

03:33:24.523 --> 03:33:28.032
Hi, I'm Garrett Houghter. Um, so I

03:33:28.532 --> 03:33:31.352
have several points that I just want to touch on really quick. Um,

03:33:31.401 --> 03:33:35.030
first, I agree with the minor increase. Um, I feel like

03:33:35.120 --> 03:33:38.666
The 220 and the 183 were just shocking, and that's literally

03:33:38.682 --> 03:33:41.459
what it was. The first time I ever saw it, I was just shocked,

03:33:42.037 --> 03:33:44.556
and then I had to come down from that, and it took a long time.

03:33:45.407 --> 03:33:49.082
Um, and with that, I just would like to condemn

03:33:49.837 --> 03:33:53.111
the comments that you all received. Um, I can

03:33:53.611 --> 03:33:56.898
only speak for myself, but I, um, every chance I get, I condemn

03:33:57.398 --> 03:34:00.060
those comments, and, uh, I'm sorry for, for that.

03:34:00.814 --> 03:34:03.877
Um, Thank you. Okay, next thing I'd like to point out,

03:34:04.021 --> 03:34:08.014
um, that class that was talked about earlier, I went

03:34:08.046 --> 03:34:11.734
to the first one and it was amazing. I really enjoyed

03:34:12.234 --> 03:34:15.534
it. I learned a lot about how the city works. Um,

03:34:15.727 --> 03:34:18.789
when they were talking about the sewer, the wastewater plant,

03:34:19.334 --> 03:34:22.589
um, I spent several hours touring and I learned a lot about that.

03:34:23.038 --> 03:34:26.983
And I think that gave me a perspective through this whole situation that a lot

03:34:27.483 --> 03:34:30.992
of other residents and citizens didn't have. I definitely encourage everyone to go

03:34:31.492 --> 03:34:34.357
to that because it gives a background that helps you,

03:34:34.632 --> 03:34:38.454
helps help me understand the projects you're talking about trying to fund.

03:34:39.679 --> 03:34:42.687
So, for everyone that's here, I recommend that 4th class that's

03:34:43.187 --> 03:34:46.498
coming up. I, um, one thing

03:34:46.530 --> 03:34:50.168
that I, you can comment to or not, but as

03:34:50.668 --> 03:34:54.193
you're talking about that new code, the 75 to 95, um, I didn't

03:34:54.693 --> 03:34:58.492
hear Anybody say that, that if it drops below that 75,

03:34:58.540 --> 03:35:01.875
that that next year it must be increased to match

03:35:01.987 --> 03:35:05.483
that, that it must be increased or should be increased, but it didn't have

03:35:05.515 --> 03:35:08.930
to go all the way up to 75 yet. And so that's something

03:35:08.962 --> 03:35:12.618
to think about. If, if you vote something much lower than that

03:35:13.131 --> 03:35:16.098
next year or the next, you have a few years to get back up to

03:35:16.598 --> 03:35:19.674
that. I didn't— it didn't sound like the code mandated

03:35:20.588 --> 03:35:23.653
huge increases the next few years. Something to think about.

03:35:24.525 --> 03:35:25.947
And then, um,

03:35:28.645 --> 03:35:31.926
oh, and then you said something. I was here this afternoon. You said something

03:35:31.942 --> 03:35:35.278
that I think is— was important for me to understand

03:35:35.521 --> 03:35:38.905
the importance of this. And I don't remember which one of you said

03:35:39.405 --> 03:35:42.525
it, but it was, um, that a lot of the sheriff's contract is

03:35:42.557 --> 03:35:45.997
being paid for by sales tax, which is

03:35:46.352 --> 03:35:50.268
variable. It fluctuates up and down. And if it goes too low,

03:35:50.989 --> 03:35:53.793
then we have to find other ways to pay for that sheriff's contract.

03:35:54.434 --> 03:35:57.463
Um, and the advantage to paying for— 8 seconds remaining.

03:35:58.120 --> 03:36:01.966
Paying for public, public safety through property taxes is that it's

03:36:01.982 --> 03:36:05.571
not variable, it's fixed. Um, and so that contract,

03:36:05.651 --> 03:36:09.801
those public safety contracts will always be covered. And I really—

03:36:10.138 --> 03:36:13.567
that was a huge perspective changer for me in this process,

03:36:14.144 --> 03:36:18.111
um, to explain why that is necessary and why property

03:36:18.611 --> 03:36:21.456
taxes need to go to public safety. So I,

03:36:22.733 --> 03:36:26.063
I'm for an increase. I personally, I,

03:36:26.903 --> 03:36:29.667
I, if I— Your time is up. Thank you.

03:36:31.941 --> 03:36:32.859
Patrick Buchanan.

03:36:43.268 --> 03:36:46.519
It's kind of hard to stand up here tonight for some personal reasons,

03:36:46.857 --> 03:36:49.690
um, but I felt the need to be here.

03:36:51.640 --> 03:36:54.838
First off, I think there's some accountability here that needs to be addressed,

03:36:55.517 --> 03:36:59.361
and I don't think this is totally resting on the back of those

03:36:59.458 --> 03:37:02.878
we elected. Personally, I think this also lands

03:37:03.378 --> 03:37:06.816
on all of us. Our driving,

03:37:07.562 --> 03:37:11.847
Which requires a lot of complaints amongst

03:37:12.347 --> 03:37:16.355
each other. Not cleaning around our houses, making sure

03:37:16.436 --> 03:37:19.637
that brush and stuff like that, that we can control.

03:37:19.993 --> 03:37:22.595
We're making a record of this. Can you speak into the mic?

03:37:23.720 --> 03:37:27.437
Brush, stuff like that, that we can control is

03:37:27.550 --> 03:37:31.592
something that we can manage. I think

03:37:32.092 --> 03:37:35.803
that I, I don't want to call out the children across the city,

03:37:35.916 --> 03:37:41.330
but I think there could be better parental

03:37:41.362 --> 03:37:44.431
type stuff going on throughout the city that reduces the demand

03:37:44.529 --> 03:37:47.839
on calls that parents could handle when it comes to law

03:37:47.872 --> 03:37:52.954
enforcement. I think that at

03:37:52.970 --> 03:37:56.918
the end of the day, when you're the one who has to call 911 and

03:37:56.950 --> 03:38:00.175
a deputy shows up, And you're thankful that they're there.

03:38:01.270 --> 03:38:05.022
It's meaningful. When you're

03:38:05.038 --> 03:38:08.428
the one who, whose home burnt down in

03:38:08.928 --> 03:38:12.820
Willow Springs, not mine, and you saw those deputies knock

03:38:12.837 --> 03:38:16.295
on every door to get everyone out, I think there's

03:38:16.795 --> 03:38:17.865
something to be said for their sacrifice.

03:38:20.399 --> 03:38:23.734
I think that when it comes to the fires that

03:38:23.783 --> 03:38:27.039
happen around this city, Whether it be the Turtle Hill fire a

03:38:27.539 --> 03:38:29.356
couple of years ago, the Lake Mountain fire.

03:38:30.927 --> 03:38:34.231
You know, there's a lot of stuff that goes into this,

03:38:35.230 --> 03:38:38.726
but there's a lot of stuff that, that we can control

03:38:38.774 --> 03:38:42.480
as citizens to kind of help reduce the demand that

03:38:42.980 --> 03:38:46.583
the city is asking for. And I think that if

03:38:46.954 --> 03:38:50.497
we're going to be a community of self-governance and elect

03:38:50.997 --> 03:38:54.265
officials to represent us, I think that they're owed the proper respect.

03:38:55.367 --> 03:38:59.122
But I also think that when

03:38:59.331 --> 03:39:02.667
the things that we need to pay for are covered, it reduces

03:39:02.780 --> 03:39:06.639
things like insurance rates and

03:39:06.655 --> 03:39:10.660
the demand that your insurance company is placing upon you and increasing

03:39:10.692 --> 03:39:13.978
your mortgage. Now, mind you, a wrap tax is

03:39:14.075 --> 03:39:17.552
great, but that's, that's tied to your sales tax.

03:39:17.633 --> 03:39:21.287
30 seconds remaining. If you are filling out

03:39:21.787 --> 03:39:25.181
a 1040, I think it's also important to remember that

03:39:25.681 --> 03:39:29.259
at the end of the year, that information is also being taken

03:39:29.759 --> 03:39:33.482
into consideration in your overall tax rate that you're paying when

03:39:33.530 --> 03:39:36.420
it comes to the federal government. And so,

03:39:37.384 --> 03:39:40.916
try to take it easy on everyone. Try to just see the other side

03:39:41.416 --> 03:39:44.995
of this and try to think that— what— ask yourself, what can I do

03:39:45.011 --> 03:39:47.339
as a citizen to make this easier? Thank you.

03:39:49.435 --> 03:39:52.955
Your time is up. Thank you. Tony Castillo.

03:40:01.430 --> 03:40:04.995
So, Tony Castillo, um, there's a lot

03:40:05.495 --> 03:40:07.287
of things I love and a lot of things I hate about Eagle Mountain.

03:40:10.410 --> 03:40:12.869
We've all been friends and we've all known each other.

03:40:14.267 --> 03:40:17.973
We've all lost friends. The biggest thing is

03:40:18.558 --> 03:40:19.273
this whole taxing.

03:40:22.750 --> 03:40:26.150
It needs to happen. My wife and I are

03:40:26.859 --> 03:40:30.162
at each other's throats over it because I'm for it, she's against it.

03:40:33.746 --> 03:40:37.121
I'd say come up with a reasonable number because a lot of us have mortgages

03:40:37.783 --> 03:40:40.932
and you guys tell us it's $25 a month extra.

03:40:41.174 --> 03:40:44.648
Yeah. Love it. Love that number. But what's not

03:40:45.148 --> 03:40:48.904
being disclosed is that our mortgage company will

03:40:48.984 --> 03:40:52.984
pay that shortage. If I only have $5,000

03:40:53.000 --> 03:40:56.132
in my escrow account and my mortgage company has to

03:40:56.632 --> 03:41:00.260
pay $300 more for that tax increase, my mortgage

03:41:00.760 --> 03:41:04.789
company is going to increase my monthly payment by

03:41:04.805 --> 03:41:08.180
double. So whatever $600 divided by 12 is, That's what they're going

03:41:08.680 --> 03:41:12.920
to charge me and every resident until the shortage

03:41:13.033 --> 03:41:16.685
has been paid in full to the mortgage company. So, as you guys

03:41:17.023 --> 03:41:20.807
look at doing this tax increase, keep, uh, bear in

03:41:21.307 --> 03:41:24.623
mind that that number that you're presenting to us is not the true number that

03:41:24.752 --> 03:41:26.602
we're going to be having to pay.

03:41:28.952 --> 03:41:32.620
Love having deputies. Um, one of

03:41:32.653 --> 03:41:35.436
the things a lot of you guys don't know is it's my first month living

03:41:35.469 --> 03:41:39.143
in Eagle Mountain back in 2020, my oldest son, who's autistic,

03:41:39.451 --> 03:41:39.955
ran away.

03:41:42.671 --> 03:41:45.661
As a dad, I'm like, what the hell?

03:41:46.792 --> 03:41:48.990
Don't know this area. My kid just ran away.

03:41:50.860 --> 03:41:54.328
And we called 911, and one of the deputies that

03:41:54.828 --> 03:41:58.410
I'd met— we'd put our kid on the list that he's a runner,

03:41:58.604 --> 03:42:02.158
all this stuff— and to see all the deputies and even the

03:42:02.238 --> 03:42:05.512
off-duty deputies come out to help look for my kid

03:42:06.973 --> 03:42:11.001
was more rewarding than anything else. So yes,

03:42:11.403 --> 03:42:14.484
everybody that is complaining about, do we, we,

03:42:14.693 --> 03:42:18.143
do we really need all this extra? Yeah, we do.

03:42:19.187 --> 03:42:21.321
We're overstretched.

03:42:22.717 --> 03:42:25.863
We want all these nice things, but we don't want to pay for it.

03:42:28.480 --> 03:42:32.173
All we got to do is come together and say, hey, let's negotiate

03:42:32.673 --> 03:42:36.813
a better, fair rate that we can all swallow. Because— 30 seconds remaining.

03:42:36.861 --> 03:42:40.265
That pill, red or blue, it's going to screw

03:42:40.281 --> 03:42:43.814
us one way or the other. It's just, if it's going to screw me

03:42:44.314 --> 03:42:47.138
over, I'd rather it be as less painful as possible. Um,

03:42:47.427 --> 03:42:49.755
that's all I gotta say, guys. Love you guys. Thank you for doing what you

03:42:50.255 --> 03:42:53.674
guys do. Apologize that you guys are getting, uh, the threats and all

03:42:54.174 --> 03:42:56.887
that stuff. Um, that's all I got to say.

03:42:59.850 --> 03:43:00.862
Betty Peralta.

03:43:03.659 --> 03:43:06.633
Betty Peralta. Good evening, my name is Betty Peralta.

03:43:20.296 --> 03:43:23.769
Unfortunately, my comments aren't going to be as nice as some of the ones you've

03:43:24.269 --> 03:43:27.926
heard. Um, I was here last week and

03:43:27.942 --> 03:43:31.518
I was very disappointed that after sitting here from

03:43:31.582 --> 03:43:34.996
6 till 11, all we heard

03:43:35.619 --> 03:43:38.744
was untruths. So here are my comments.

03:43:40.149 --> 03:43:44.398
You've already made a decision. The resolution to increase the taxes

03:43:45.042 --> 03:43:48.591
regardless of the overwhelming opposition by the citizens

03:43:48.607 --> 03:43:51.865
of Eagle Mountain, has gone on deaf ears.

03:43:53.090 --> 03:43:56.371
Rumor has it that this council has already decided on a new

03:43:56.500 --> 03:43:59.879
number without listening to what we have to say.

03:44:01.569 --> 03:44:04.134
You were elected for the representation of the citizens,

03:44:04.795 --> 03:44:08.408
not to make closed-door decisions and lying

03:44:08.908 --> 03:44:12.549
and misrepresenting What the expected new funds

03:44:12.902 --> 03:44:16.486
would cover. I've asked 3 times

03:44:16.518 --> 03:44:19.574
for a line item budget. I still have to see it.

03:44:20.213 --> 03:44:24.036
I've received no answers. This council

03:44:24.536 --> 03:44:27.881
is deaf to the voices of the people that you, that you represent.

03:44:28.705 --> 03:44:31.791
You were hired by the citizens, and it's expected

03:44:32.509 --> 03:44:35.598
that you do just that, represent us.

03:44:36.504 --> 03:44:39.443
And stop working for your own personal interests.

03:44:40.760 --> 03:44:44.583
And stop making frivolous plans that are not priorities.

03:44:45.483 --> 03:44:49.514
As I mentioned to you last week, I come from 38

03:44:50.014 --> 03:44:53.305
years of public safety. I was a first responder.

03:44:53.915 --> 03:44:57.449
I know that that's critical, and I know that having police is critical.

03:44:58.895 --> 03:45:01.369
But your excuses, your sad stories.

03:45:01.964 --> 03:45:05.731
Will fall on deaf ears, just like our voices have

03:45:06.231 --> 03:45:09.385
fallen on your deaf ears. And I don't

03:45:09.450 --> 03:45:13.373
see any compassion for the people that were up here, the elderly,

03:45:13.891 --> 03:45:16.352
the retired that are on fixed incomes.

03:45:17.730 --> 03:45:21.526
You continue to live well with all of the perks that your positions

03:45:21.559 --> 03:45:24.749
provide. And none of you have to worry about

03:45:24.863 --> 03:45:27.464
high gas prices because the city provides you a car.

03:45:28.245 --> 03:45:31.975
All of us don't have that perk. I said,

03:45:32.300 --> 03:45:35.917
please don't patronize us citizens with your excuses

03:45:36.841 --> 03:45:39.566
of not doing your job effectively and that you will try better.

03:45:40.613 --> 03:45:43.657
Try downsizing your lifestyle. That's what you've told us.

03:45:44.956 --> 03:45:48.644
Expenses for many Eagle Mountain

03:45:48.757 --> 03:45:53.557
residents— 30 seconds remaining. Are— I'm sorry, that is exactly

03:45:53.590 --> 03:45:56.751
what Eagle Mountain citizens are doing on a daily basis.

03:45:57.653 --> 03:46:01.310
Eagle Mountain citizens' hard-earned money is

03:46:01.358 --> 03:46:04.248
not for your discretionary or personal use. Thank you.

03:46:07.631 --> 03:46:10.559
David Higgins, I think, is what it says. Is that right?

03:46:15.896 --> 03:46:19.661
Yeah, David Higgins. Yes, ma'am. Is that correct? Okay. Higgins.

03:46:19.712 --> 03:46:23.587
Okay. Yep. Thanks. Good evening.

03:46:25.469 --> 03:46:29.185
I first would like to thank you guys for this opportunity for me

03:46:29.877 --> 03:46:33.780
to vent and express my feelings on this,

03:46:35.526 --> 03:46:38.371
uh, tax increase. But first of all and foremost,

03:46:39.050 --> 03:46:42.066
I'm acting liaison for Eagle Mountain's 3

03:46:42.566 --> 03:46:46.471
percenters. Do you guys know what that is? That's your seniors

03:46:47.294 --> 03:46:50.099
and your fixed incomes. That's me.

03:46:51.328 --> 03:46:53.606
And 3% makes us the minority.

03:46:55.420 --> 03:46:58.920
So anyway, but thank you again, and I have to admit this,

03:46:58.984 --> 03:47:02.437
that I myself are in disagreement with

03:47:03.195 --> 03:47:07.139
the tax hike. I'm more for the referendum than against

03:47:07.639 --> 03:47:10.626
it. The reason for that is, is my,

03:47:11.172 --> 03:47:14.659
my views are that it should be fairness for all.

03:47:15.102 --> 03:47:18.717
by all. And in order to obtain something like

03:47:19.217 --> 03:47:23.199
that, we need to put it on a ballot and have a vote and

03:47:23.280 --> 03:47:26.442
have that. Now, ballots used to be pretty secure at one time.

03:47:26.782 --> 03:47:29.746
I'm not saying they're that way anymore, but, uh,

03:47:31.301 --> 03:47:33.696
that's where I stand. And, uh, once again,

03:47:35.343 --> 03:47:38.865
I'm not in favor of the hike, and it's not because I don't think taxes

03:47:38.962 --> 03:47:43.561
aren't needed. It's because I think it's the way we require And

03:47:43.593 --> 03:47:46.871
obtain those taxes that needs to be polished.

03:47:47.355 --> 03:47:48.098
Anyway, thank you.

03:47:50.553 --> 03:47:51.253
Donna Burnham.

03:47:58.648 --> 03:48:02.159
First of all, I want to say how horrified I

03:48:02.207 --> 03:48:05.299
am by the things that Melissa Clark read.

03:48:07.038 --> 03:48:10.368
That should never have happened. And I want

03:48:10.868 --> 03:48:14.366
you to know that you don't deserve that. Um,

03:48:14.625 --> 03:48:17.924
I understand what it's like to be in those seats because I sat in

03:48:17.941 --> 03:48:21.369
them for 16 years, and it's a

03:48:21.869 --> 03:48:25.639
heavy load. And I know how hard all of you work, so I

03:48:26.139 --> 03:48:28.616
just want you to know you didn't deserve any of that,

03:48:29.198 --> 03:48:33.378
and I'm sorry that we weren't better that

03:48:33.878 --> 03:48:37.615
we needed to be. I believe you want the best for the city. I do

03:48:38.115 --> 03:48:40.392
take issue with a few things, and one of them, of course, is going to

03:48:40.505 --> 03:48:43.988
be the blame put on former councils. Um,

03:48:44.598 --> 03:48:48.322
I feel like it's very important that we be good stewards

03:48:48.822 --> 03:48:51.757
of the tax dollars, and I feel like I was a good steward of our

03:48:52.257 --> 03:48:55.064
tax dollars. We were lean, um,

03:48:56.171 --> 03:48:58.515
and that's what we should be. We should be lean.

03:48:59.365 --> 03:49:02.158
However, in the last few years, we became too lean.

03:49:03.313 --> 03:49:06.857
And I get that. And should we have raised taxes?

03:49:06.937 --> 03:49:10.113
Maybe. But we were also raising utility rates, as you remember,

03:49:10.449 --> 03:49:14.426
which was a huge impact on citizens. People were reeling from

03:49:14.458 --> 03:49:18.066
the cost from COVID and from all other things. So that's

03:49:18.566 --> 03:49:21.995
why we didn't— we didn't put that burden on the residents because

03:49:22.059 --> 03:49:25.330
we knew that there was a bright future ahead.

03:49:25.924 --> 03:49:29.275
And we, we took a risk that that would come sooner than later.

03:49:30.269 --> 03:49:33.105
So I get that you're in a position that's difficult,

03:49:33.602 --> 03:49:37.304
um, but yes, we have a smaller percentage of

03:49:37.804 --> 03:49:41.166
the sheriff's department than other cities do, um, but our call

03:49:41.214 --> 03:49:44.643
times have always been good until the last few years.

03:49:45.220 --> 03:49:48.842
And call times are what matters. It matters how long it takes

03:49:49.342 --> 03:49:53.233
a deputy to get to your house. That's what matters. And so yeah,

03:49:53.329 --> 03:49:56.890
we need more officers, especially Especially with the increase in calls.

03:49:56.938 --> 03:50:00.246
That's obvious. I get that. And so do we

03:50:00.746 --> 03:50:04.710
need an increase? Probably. Do we need that

03:50:05.210 --> 03:50:08.644
significant an increase? I don't think so. And I, I would

03:50:09.144 --> 03:50:12.995
respectfully ask that you look at just doing maybe a 50% increase.

03:50:14.424 --> 03:50:18.583
And I know that's a risk because I'm asking you to

03:50:18.695 --> 03:50:22.514
bet on future income. But I think you all know it's coming

03:50:23.027 --> 03:50:26.683
and that it's there. And I think that that's a risk worth

03:50:26.715 --> 03:50:30.612
taking to protect our vulnerable citizens, those in

03:50:30.644 --> 03:50:34.621
the 3%, as he was talking about. Also families with children

03:50:34.733 --> 03:50:38.068
who— young families who are just struggling to make ends

03:50:38.164 --> 03:50:42.173
meet, that don't have insurance or whatever. So that would

03:50:42.673 --> 03:50:46.375
be what I would ask. And I appreciate you at least

03:50:46.439 --> 03:50:50.716
being willing to repeal what you started with and at least listening to

03:50:51.216 --> 03:50:55.160
our concerns. Thank you. Michael Thompson.

03:51:02.049 --> 03:51:05.616
Hello, I'm a 9-year resident of Eagle Mountain, and I appreciate

03:51:05.681 --> 03:51:08.022
all that you do. And,

03:51:09.395 --> 03:51:12.690
uh, I want you to know that I'm also a great supporter of, of our

03:51:13.190 --> 03:51:16.518
first responders, my own Father-in-law and brother-in-law

03:51:16.679 --> 03:51:19.719
are retired Utah police officers, and,

03:51:20.786 --> 03:51:23.925
and I, I want to see more support for them,

03:51:25.663 --> 03:51:27.187
and, and I'm willing to pay for it.

03:51:29.824 --> 03:51:30.419
That said,

03:51:34.172 --> 03:51:37.747
I could add to the hardship stories. I have plenty of my

03:51:37.780 --> 03:51:41.030
own, including a daughter that lives here and is,

03:51:41.371 --> 03:51:44.117
is scared to death that her rent's about to go up because of the tax

03:51:44.617 --> 03:51:47.975
increase. But what I really want to do is see

03:51:48.475 --> 03:51:51.998
if I can offer some help. So I have a stepson who

03:51:52.498 --> 03:51:55.086
is a construction manager for custom homes in Salem.

03:51:56.225 --> 03:52:00.993
He tells me that they enacted a $30,000 charge

03:52:01.122 --> 03:52:05.463
for new building permits. They do that to slow growth

03:52:06.851 --> 03:52:11.527
and to provide money so that infrastructure can be put in place before the

03:52:11.543 --> 03:52:14.993
growth occurs. And I think maybe we need to look at the

03:52:15.493 --> 03:52:17.689
possibility of doing that. Um,

03:52:19.069 --> 03:52:21.604
and I, I would much rather see us, uh,

03:52:22.037 --> 03:52:25.471
get some more money out of these developers like Carl Ivory,

03:52:25.503 --> 03:52:29.515
who, by the way, has raised my HOA fees 350%

03:52:30.015 --> 03:52:33.606
since I moved into my house 5 years ago. And I'd like to see

03:52:34.106 --> 03:52:37.730
the city do something to stop them from— these declarant-controlled HOAs

03:52:37.762 --> 03:52:40.943
are out of control. The other thing is,

03:52:41.362 --> 03:52:45.509
I ask that you quit giving a break in water rates to residents

03:52:45.574 --> 03:52:49.296
with lots that are over half an acre versus the rest

03:52:49.796 --> 03:52:53.060
of us. I know there were some good reasons

03:52:53.108 --> 03:52:56.429
for doing that in the past. I think those times have passed,

03:52:56.912 --> 03:52:59.636
and they should be paying the same rates as the rest of us and get

03:53:00.136 --> 03:53:03.327
some more money for the water that, that is used in the

03:53:03.827 --> 03:53:05.819
city. That's all I have to add. Thank you.

03:53:09.012 --> 03:53:09.721
Duncan Searcy.

03:53:17.140 --> 03:53:19.932
Melissa, you can take a breath. I'm here for Craig tonight, not you.

03:53:20.803 --> 03:53:23.789
But I do want to say I'm sorry that you have received death threats,

03:53:23.934 --> 03:53:27.709
um, and publicly condemn that. And I'm serious. I've been

03:53:27.741 --> 03:53:30.858
on the receiving end of, of that before in my life, and it is not

03:53:31.358 --> 03:53:34.818
a fun feeling, and it's not appropriate. So I, I'm, I'm sorry

03:53:34.850 --> 03:53:38.977
that some of the content that I've generated has caused you to feel that uncomfortable

03:53:39.282 --> 03:53:42.381
stuff. I unfortunately cannot, you know,

03:53:42.461 --> 03:53:45.689
regulate how people react to the things that I say, but I

03:53:46.189 --> 03:53:48.932
am sorry that you experienced that. And I hope you know that, um, you are

03:53:48.980 --> 03:53:52.882
still my sister in Christ and you deserve to be safe and happy,

03:53:53.621 --> 03:53:56.318
even though we very seldom agree on things. I,

03:53:56.591 --> 03:54:00.220
I— that's not appropriate. So, um, I'll give you your

03:54:00.720 --> 03:54:03.350
time. I'm just gonna remind you, personal attacks will not be accepted.

03:54:04.540 --> 03:54:07.780
So speak as you will. Have I made a personal attack? You said I'm here

03:54:08.280 --> 03:54:11.860
after Craig. Well, I'm gonna give Craig some feedback about the truth in taxation.

03:54:12.360 --> 03:54:15.360
I'm okay with feedback. I don't want an attack, if that's okay. Okay. Uh,

03:54:15.860 --> 03:54:18.580
so where are we at on time then? Where were we at when, when I

03:54:19.080 --> 03:54:22.600
got interrupted? We paused it. You have 2 minutes. Yep. All right, I'll keep going.

03:54:22.880 --> 03:54:25.490
Um, and then I just want to say thank you to my fellow citizens.

03:54:25.560 --> 03:54:27.900
I didn't think I would get to speak tonight because I had other engagements.

03:54:29.817 --> 03:54:34.143
And so I want to thank

03:54:34.643 --> 03:54:36.868
you for doing that. I know it's not easy to stand up here and speak

03:54:37.368 --> 03:54:40.858
your mind, but it is very important. And then I also owe an apology

03:54:40.954 --> 03:54:44.335
to, to the mayor, Jared Gray. Um, he caught some

03:54:44.835 --> 03:54:48.245
heat from my social media today because I'm being investigated by the

03:54:48.745 --> 03:54:51.979
Utah County Sheriff's Office, uh, because somebody here on the dais— it's not

03:54:52.091 --> 03:54:54.735
Jared Gray— uh, said that I'm making threats. Thank you.

03:54:56.099 --> 03:54:59.422
And so, uh, I, I, I thought that was you,

03:54:59.727 --> 03:55:03.017
but after we got into the discussion, we discovered that it's actually

03:55:03.517 --> 03:55:06.917
somebody else, not you. So I apologize, and I'm more than happy to

03:55:06.933 --> 03:55:09.083
put out another video. I hope you'll do that with me, and we can,

03:55:09.517 --> 03:55:13.850
we can set the record straight that that wasn't you that's, uh, using law

03:55:13.914 --> 03:55:18.199
enforcement as a pressure to try and silence me. Um, so now

03:55:18.699 --> 03:55:21.553
we'll get to Craig's feedback, not attacks. Okay,

03:55:21.939 --> 03:55:25.519
so for the Truth in Taxation meeting, I was there. You started

03:55:25.631 --> 03:55:29.904
off with saying that we needed speed tables and

03:55:30.048 --> 03:55:33.486
the discussion went to child safety. Okay, for me, that's gaslighting.

03:55:33.823 --> 03:55:37.662
We're not— that's not what we're there to talk about. Then you shifted

03:55:38.162 --> 03:55:41.838
our discussion to Fauci and you stopped trying to

03:55:42.031 --> 03:55:44.955
appeal to people's love of children.

03:55:45.147 --> 03:55:48.488
And then we're going to try and deflect the anger to Fauci. That's not why.

03:55:49.018 --> 03:55:52.611
Trust me, dude. I lost a pretty sweet career in part because

03:55:53.111 --> 03:55:55.865
of the policies that that man put out. I hate the guy. Okay. 30 seconds.

03:55:55.913 --> 03:55:59.456
But the fact that you're going to try and deflect anger to Fauci instead of

03:55:59.956 --> 03:56:03.256
staying on, on task is totally inappropriate. And then the last one

03:56:03.288 --> 03:56:07.071
is the biggest one. I'm a war veteran. Never ever

03:56:07.279 --> 03:56:11.111
would I use people's ultimate sacrifice as an

03:56:11.143 --> 03:56:14.910
example of you're going to be our general and we need to fix bayonets

03:56:15.410 --> 03:56:18.810
and go into battle. Especially over taxes. A lot of our brave men

03:56:18.843 --> 03:56:21.328
and women have died because of taxes.

03:56:22.360 --> 03:56:26.140
So please do not ever do that again. Thank you.

03:56:27.121 --> 03:56:30.536
Your time is up. Thank you. Kristen Meyer.

03:56:37.710 --> 03:56:41.006
Hi, good evening. I'm Kristen Meyer.

03:56:41.562 --> 03:56:44.889
On August 6th, I gave a comment to urge the

03:56:45.389 --> 03:56:49.588
city to lower the proposed tax rate to cover only the $1.5 million contract

03:56:49.620 --> 03:56:52.971
for the sheriff's office, because I support public safety.

03:56:53.870 --> 03:56:57.654
Um, and I was really hopeful because you did lower the tax amount to

03:56:58.154 --> 03:57:00.364
183%, and that's progress.

03:57:01.246 --> 03:57:04.582
Um, still not quite there, but I was hopeful when I heard

03:57:04.614 --> 03:57:08.559
that a group of residents met and the city negotiated a

03:57:09.059 --> 03:57:12.569
new rate again. Um, I downloaded the agenda packet

03:57:12.633 --> 03:57:16.034
and I pulled the resolution, and there were blank spaces for the

03:57:16.534 --> 03:57:19.643
new tax rate and the percentage amount and the dollar amount.

03:57:19.707 --> 03:57:23.156
So it was hard to prepare for a public comment because I couldn't see it

03:57:23.656 --> 03:57:26.237
beforehand before this meeting. So that would have been more helpful.

03:57:27.231 --> 03:57:30.456
Um, and then I just wanted to say, I understand, like,

03:57:30.520 --> 03:57:33.889
the city has needs beyond the sheriff's contract. Um,

03:57:33.969 --> 03:57:37.404
costs are up for everybody, but incomes aren't rising to

03:57:37.420 --> 03:57:40.954
keep up with that. Um, layoffs are

03:57:41.454 --> 03:57:45.453
extensive, as you know, and then people who do keep their

03:57:45.953 --> 03:57:49.390
jobs are told that, um, they can't get a raise and

03:57:49.890 --> 03:57:53.375
that you should just be grateful to have a job. So with our income not

03:57:53.439 --> 03:57:56.331
rising, it's hard to keep up with, like, the costs.

03:57:57.102 --> 03:58:01.344
Um, and I also want to just be mindful about the Tyson's plant being closed

03:58:01.376 --> 03:58:05.164
and leaving families without a job. So, um,

03:58:05.875 --> 03:58:09.524
I would support it if the tax rate just covers the

03:58:10.024 --> 03:58:13.491
cost of the sheriff's, uh, county contract. Thanks.

03:58:17.128 --> 03:58:17.972
Jeff Ruth.

03:58:35.950 --> 03:58:38.724
Hey guys, um, I wasn't planning on speaking tonight,

03:58:39.894 --> 03:58:44.030
but let me start by saying the roll-on of this sucked.

03:58:45.007 --> 03:58:48.759
Um, could have done much better. Uh, I've known

03:58:48.791 --> 03:58:52.237
you all pretty much except for Zach over here.

03:58:53.183 --> 03:58:56.458
Uh, I remember Jared and

03:58:56.490 --> 03:58:59.912
me when he was first running for office, talking on my front porch.

03:59:01.294 --> 03:59:05.006
You got to put your trust in something. Got to put my trust in you

03:59:05.506 --> 03:59:08.782
guys because you guys are the ones that are looking at the numbers. And then

03:59:09.282 --> 03:59:13.088
I see these people, like one guy at the last meeting,

03:59:14.309 --> 03:59:18.359
that Pony Express isn't safe for his motorcycle when he's

03:59:18.407 --> 03:59:22.100
riding. Well, Yeah, I was thinking about it today

03:59:22.600 --> 03:59:26.016
coming down, and yeah, that road is rough. And I've seen other people saying,

03:59:26.049 --> 03:59:28.456
well, why didn't they just, you know, repave it?

03:59:29.403 --> 03:59:32.548
Well, because that costs a lot of money. Um, but they

03:59:33.048 --> 03:59:36.143
don't want to pay for that part, but they complain when it gets, you know,

03:59:36.159 --> 03:59:39.706
to make the road itself last longer, that gets crack sealed.

03:59:40.557 --> 03:59:43.927
Um, it's just some of the things people come up

03:59:44.427 --> 03:59:47.796
with that we need this, we need this, we need this. But then

03:59:48.296 --> 03:59:50.766
when you guys try to figure out how to do all that, they don't want

03:59:51.266 --> 03:59:55.085
to pay for it. And I've been on the end, like I said at

03:59:55.585 --> 03:59:58.634
the last meeting, waiting for a sheriff's deputy to show up.

03:59:59.902 --> 04:00:03.435
Um, I've had a neighbor threatening me and my wife,

04:00:04.880 --> 04:00:07.963
and we had to wait a little bit for a deputy to get there.

04:00:08.749 --> 04:00:11.848
And you know what he told me? Hey, you better be carrying.

04:00:12.974 --> 04:00:16.122
Because they knew those people. Um,

04:00:16.992 --> 04:00:20.681
and minor things I've called in and

04:00:20.713 --> 04:00:23.806
I get a phone call, hey, we can't come out today, we only got 2

04:00:23.919 --> 04:00:26.918
officers working this morning. Okay, I understand,

04:00:28.596 --> 04:00:31.790
but I believe you'll do the right thing.

04:00:32.867 --> 04:00:36.079
I believe you are concerned about the citizens.

04:00:36.715 --> 04:00:39.774
You guys know I'm on disability. My pay isn't going to go

04:00:39.919 --> 04:00:42.342
up. It's going to be a little bit more rough.

04:00:43.424 --> 04:00:45.426
So do what's right.

04:00:47.025 --> 04:00:47.849
Think it over hard.

04:00:49.646 --> 04:00:52.131
And I'll support you guys.

04:00:53.599 --> 04:00:57.325
It, it's hard out there. It ain't going

04:00:57.825 --> 04:01:00.552
to get any easier. But we need things done in this city,

04:01:01.389 --> 04:01:05.327
like Pony Express fixed. Try drinking coffee

04:01:05.408 --> 04:01:09.116
on that road without getting it up your nose. Seconds remaining.

04:01:09.553 --> 04:01:13.596
So I wish you guys would tell the people that,

04:01:14.160 --> 04:01:17.815
like, for the new city hall that's being planned, hey, we need to get

04:01:19.135 --> 04:01:22.719
our employees under one roof instead of having them scattered all over

04:01:23.362 --> 04:01:28.108
and paying rent for these buildings. So again,

04:01:28.368 --> 04:01:31.268
thank you. Do what's right. Think of us.

04:01:32.385 --> 04:01:33.058
Have a good night.

04:01:36.630 --> 04:01:38.113
Tracy Peretta.

04:01:43.757 --> 04:01:47.032
I'm gonna bring buckets of feathers. Speak to

04:01:47.048 --> 04:01:50.340
the mic. Sorry. I was gonna bring in a bucket of tar and some feathers.

04:01:50.518 --> 04:01:53.180
Thought it'd be funny. I'm glad you didn't. Yeah, you might think it's a threat.

04:01:53.293 --> 04:01:57.756
It wasn't a threat. It was just to be funny. So one

04:01:57.869 --> 04:02:01.186
thing that I have an issue with is he's complaining about, uh,

04:02:01.508 --> 04:02:04.681
Pioneer— or excuse me, Pony Express. Wasn't it paved last year?

04:02:07.427 --> 04:02:10.940
Yes, I rode my bike on it last year. It was a crack

04:02:11.005 --> 04:02:13.627
seal treatment. It was a preventative maintenance treatment.

04:02:13.935 --> 04:02:17.029
I'll talk to you about it after, but it was different than—

04:02:17.077 --> 04:02:19.046
Have somebody come back and fix it if it's not adequate.

04:02:20.739 --> 04:02:24.868
Don't pay for service if it's not what it's supposed to be. If everybody's complaining

04:02:25.368 --> 04:02:29.026
about it, it needs to be done right the first time. Ask somebody to come

04:02:29.058 --> 04:02:31.472
back and fix the problem if it's inadequate.

04:02:32.438 --> 04:02:34.899
The other thing is, you guys have all been on the board for a long

04:02:34.932 --> 04:02:38.403
time. Donna was on the board. All I ever heard at

04:02:38.661 --> 04:02:42.058
every meeting I came to, I objected to it. Let's just build,

04:02:42.122 --> 04:02:44.746
build, build. You guys were like drunken sailors.

04:02:44.939 --> 04:02:48.238
Seriously, it was bad. I said, don't spend your water rights.

04:02:48.482 --> 04:02:51.478
Why are we giving water to everybody? And that's all that you guys did.

04:02:52.032 --> 04:02:55.433
And it was ridiculous. So you built, you brought all these people

04:02:55.465 --> 04:02:58.834
out here. Everybody came out here because it was cheap. This is

04:02:59.334 --> 04:03:02.588
the only place they could afford. Now they're out here and you're going,

04:03:02.636 --> 04:03:05.507
oh, now you're going to have to pay all these taxes. Too bad we grew

04:03:06.007 --> 04:03:09.581
too fast. Well, you guys didn't put in the infrastructure for

04:03:09.678 --> 04:03:13.014
businesses to be able to have a tax base that we can rely on.

04:03:13.672 --> 04:03:17.025
All our tax money goes down to Saratoga Springs. They go down to

04:03:17.041 --> 04:03:21.047
the Walmart, they go down to the Costco. I mean, it's called retail

04:03:21.160 --> 04:03:24.225
leakage. All our money goes there instead of

04:03:24.725 --> 04:03:27.726
bringing it into our community and spending it. I've been here for 10 years.

04:03:27.774 --> 04:03:31.781
We're just now getting businesses here on the street. It's ridiculous.

04:03:33.591 --> 04:03:37.244
You guys have put the cart way before the horse, and you needed to

04:03:37.293 --> 04:03:40.775
stop and think about that. So,

04:03:41.713 --> 04:03:44.332
the other issue that I had— I'm sorry, I gotta look at my notes.

04:03:47.748 --> 04:03:51.178
So everybody says that we need more money for the police department. We have so

04:03:51.678 --> 04:03:55.859
many military here. We have not a huge retirement

04:03:56.359 --> 04:04:00.203
community, but we have some elderly people here. Why don't we have a citizen volunteer

04:04:00.571 --> 04:04:02.960
that can go do the stupid calls that, you know,

04:04:04.258 --> 04:04:07.993
kids riding down the street without a helmet on, or he's riding an e-bike.

04:04:08.410 --> 04:04:12.002
Those are things that can be taken care of by a citizen patrol. Instead of

04:04:12.355 --> 04:04:15.647
taxing our police force to go out and do the piddly stuff,

04:04:16.209 --> 04:04:19.243
because they're going to come to my neighborhood and they're going to bring 2 police

04:04:19.743 --> 04:04:22.936
officers and they're going to have all their cars there just to ask one little

04:04:23.436 --> 04:04:26.790
kid, you know, where's your helmet? Because I've seen it. We passed it last week.

04:04:27.127 --> 04:04:30.627
We— 30 seconds remaining. We went down the street. They had

04:04:30.724 --> 04:04:34.192
3 police cars pulling one person over. I mean, how many people does it

04:04:34.692 --> 04:04:38.065
take to screw in a light bulb? Seriously. It's getting

04:04:38.278 --> 04:04:41.707
a little bit ridiculous. We really have

04:04:42.207 --> 04:04:45.466
a low crime area, and we need to take advantage of that. Ask the citizens

04:04:45.498 --> 04:04:48.821
to help volunteer to take up some of the load and not spend all our

04:04:49.321 --> 04:04:49.890
money. Thank you.

04:04:53.136 --> 04:04:54.100
Melody Castillo.

04:05:01.967 --> 04:05:05.246
Sorry for my appearance. I was getting my kids ready for school

04:05:05.262 --> 04:05:07.900
tomorrow and had to run down here. Um,

04:05:08.477 --> 04:05:12.386
because like a few other people have said, I have been horrified

04:05:13.684 --> 04:05:16.904
by the things that have been said to you guys, and that is absolutely not

04:05:17.404 --> 04:05:20.829
okay. And I feel like it's creating this divisiveness within

04:05:21.329 --> 04:05:23.521
our— within our, our amazing city.

04:05:24.738 --> 04:05:28.359
And this us versus them mentality— people forget you guys live

04:05:28.859 --> 04:05:33.134
in this city too. You're voting for or against or whatever taxes

04:05:33.262 --> 04:05:36.546
that you— that affect you as well. And I think people forget

04:05:37.046 --> 04:05:40.403
that sometimes. Thank you. Um, so I'm so sorry that you're dealing with

04:05:40.903 --> 04:05:44.673
all of that, because whether I agree with you or not, I know that

04:05:44.721 --> 04:05:48.417
in your hearts you love this city, you love the people of this city,

04:05:49.337 --> 04:05:52.614
and you're doing the best that you can.

04:05:53.114 --> 04:05:56.239
And so I applaud you guys for that. Um,

04:05:56.899 --> 04:06:00.426
second, I apologize to

04:06:00.539 --> 04:06:03.756
every other entity In the

04:06:04.256 --> 04:06:08.149
city, I don't care what you say. We have the best deputies out

04:06:08.262 --> 04:06:12.929
here. Our law enforcement out here is amazing, and I'm

04:06:12.930 --> 04:06:16.251
coming from one who I used to be on the side

04:06:16.751 --> 04:06:20.443
of we need our own police force, and I don't think

04:06:20.943 --> 04:06:21.798
we can do any better than what we have.

04:06:24.265 --> 04:06:27.975
I see what they go through. They're stretched

04:06:28.475 --> 04:06:32.347
thin, and in what? What other industry,

04:06:33.581 --> 04:06:37.173
when you're good at your job, good at your job, do you get punished

04:06:38.963 --> 04:06:42.770
by not getting the support that you need, not getting the help that you need?

04:06:43.336 --> 04:06:47.251
So I am in favor of an

04:06:47.365 --> 04:06:51.011
increase, but I think

04:06:51.511 --> 04:06:54.972
that they're going to get the short end of the stick because so many people

04:06:55.005 --> 04:06:57.960
are upset. upset about the additional stuff.

04:06:58.958 --> 04:07:02.162
And I think that we need to make sure that

04:07:02.259 --> 04:07:05.595
we don't sacrifice the needs of our

04:07:05.741 --> 04:07:09.171
deputies out here in order to get everything else.

04:07:10.012 --> 04:07:12.714
Um, so yeah, that's it.

04:07:15.803 --> 04:07:18.879
Um, it looks like Wade S is here. I called him earlier, but he was

04:07:18.976 --> 04:07:19.904
not here. Is he here now?

04:07:26.361 --> 04:07:29.750
Thank you for the— for giving me time. Um, I haven't been here as

04:07:29.847 --> 04:07:33.185
long as most people. I've only been here a few months. I moved here

04:07:33.396 --> 04:07:36.745
a few months ago to be closer to family and help out. Um,

04:07:37.052 --> 04:07:39.722
but I wanted to start out by saying that, uh,

04:07:41.502 --> 04:07:45.367
why, uh, God created police officers is

04:07:45.399 --> 04:07:46.828
so firemen could have heroes.

04:07:50.993 --> 04:07:54.922
So I'm,

04:07:55.132 --> 04:07:57.459
I'm a retired police officer, and so I support,

04:07:58.834 --> 04:08:02.324
I support, I support the,

04:08:02.405 --> 04:08:05.638
the tax for them, um, because we

04:08:06.138 --> 04:08:09.144
need that. We're growing, we're growing fast, um,

04:08:09.884 --> 04:08:13.201
and again, I, I do thank each of you for serving in the capacities

04:08:13.234 --> 04:08:16.971
that you do. I'm sure it's not easy, but I,

04:08:17.036 --> 04:08:20.112
but I do appreciate that. I think that to go back to the table and

04:08:20.612 --> 04:08:24.998
reevaluate the other taxes, because we need to get some itemized,

04:08:25.612 --> 04:08:28.911
you know, something, some kind of list showing us where this is going.

04:08:29.655 --> 04:08:32.277
I love it here already. I plan on being here for a while.

04:08:33.137 --> 04:08:36.610
And yeah, just thank you. Thank you for the opportunity for

04:08:36.643 --> 04:08:40.129
being here. Okay,

04:08:40.194 --> 04:08:43.279
these last couple we received through the recorder's office earlier today. Just want to see

04:08:43.779 --> 04:08:49.044
if they are here. Courtney Ramirez stated,

04:08:49.141 --> 04:08:51.939
please listen to the residents who are asking you not to raise our property taxes.

04:08:52.678 --> 04:08:55.682
And since Charlotte is here, we can just go to you, Charlotte Ducos.

04:08:58.236 --> 04:08:59.849
Sorry, I just didn't want to walk in front of everybody.

04:09:02.700 --> 04:09:06.297
I teach at the high school, so I have an early morning tomorrow,

04:09:07.013 --> 04:09:10.420
but I teach government, and one of

04:09:10.920 --> 04:09:12.909
the projects that I do with my students is they take a look at our

04:09:13.409 --> 04:09:16.682
city budget every semester. And I'm grateful

04:09:17.182 --> 04:09:20.841
for the partnership with the city putting that information together. And one

04:09:21.341 --> 04:09:23.795
of my favorite moments is when they take a look at the spreadsheet and realize

04:09:23.891 --> 04:09:26.878
how little money they have for the list of projects that they have to do.

04:09:26.926 --> 04:09:30.394
And these are actual projects. And they look at me like, how are you supposed

04:09:30.894 --> 04:09:33.509
to do this? I'm like, that's a great question. Um, you're, you're elected leaders.

04:09:33.686 --> 04:09:37.469
have to figure that out every single year. And, um, if high

04:09:37.969 --> 04:09:41.364
schoolers can figure it out, um, by looking at those numbers,

04:09:41.476 --> 04:09:45.131
then I think that we need to learn to do the same thing. And,

04:09:45.387 --> 04:09:48.834
uh, the interesting thing is I've been working this budget project for

04:09:49.334 --> 04:09:52.777
years now, and some of the same projects are on the list

04:09:53.277 --> 04:09:57.025
that were there when we started looking at this project. And,

04:09:57.330 --> 04:10:00.873
um, Donna mentioned— and Donna and I are good friends Um,

04:10:01.114 --> 04:10:04.470
and Donna mentioned that, um, they ran lean and

04:10:04.970 --> 04:10:07.280
they did it on purpose because that's how it should be, and I don't disagree

04:10:07.780 --> 04:10:11.133
with that. Um, she also said, were we maybe too lean? Um,

04:10:11.551 --> 04:10:15.404
that's where, that's where her and I disagree a little bit. I think they were

04:10:15.904 --> 04:10:20.414
too lean. I think, uh, government's responsibility is to meet the needs and,

04:10:21.088 --> 04:10:24.380
and hoping for income that's maybe going to come and

04:10:24.880 --> 04:10:28.347
hopefully next year Um, that's like paying with a credit card.

04:10:28.556 --> 04:10:32.235
We— if we don't have that income yet, we're not— like, we, we have

04:10:32.267 --> 04:10:36.220
to do something about it. And I appreciate that

04:10:36.720 --> 04:10:39.256
the council has taken the time to listen to the residents and to bring the

04:10:39.756 --> 04:10:43.562
number down. Um, I think that that's appropriate, but I, I do think that

04:10:43.739 --> 04:10:47.675
we need that tax increase. Um, we don't have to get all of those projects,

04:10:47.755 --> 04:10:51.740
and we are not going to. Um, the 0.9 that's being— that's on

04:10:51.772 --> 04:10:55.175
the table right now Um, is, is not

04:10:55.207 --> 04:10:58.273
going to cover even a drop in

04:10:58.773 --> 04:11:01.645
the bucket of those projects that have been on the list for years and years

04:11:01.678 --> 04:11:03.874
and years. But I think we got to start somewhere.

04:11:04.652 --> 04:11:07.876
Um, and I think that officers and employees

04:11:07.990 --> 04:11:10.647
to meet the needs of the city that we already have— it doesn't even buy

04:11:11.147 --> 04:11:13.632
anything new, just allows us to do the things we're already funding.

04:11:14.462 --> 04:11:17.458
Um, I think, I think that that's probably a great place to start.

04:11:19.491 --> 04:11:23.046
And, and that's, that's the comment that I wanted to make tonight.

04:11:26.610 --> 04:11:30.096
This is another email comment that came in. John J., you're here.

04:11:32.168 --> 04:11:35.526
He just states, I do not feel there's justification with the tax increase.

04:11:35.574 --> 04:11:37.868
It's rather lengthy, so I'll make sure it's part of the record and get you

04:11:38.368 --> 04:11:40.774
a copy as well. Jason Clint emailed.

04:11:44.695 --> 04:11:48.452
Another one believes that there's a more reasonable approach to

04:11:48.952 --> 04:11:52.482
approve a tax increase that covers additional expense associated with the sheriff's contracts.

04:11:53.430 --> 04:11:56.754
Let's see, this one is also rather lengthy, so I can make sure.

04:11:57.765 --> 04:12:01.009
He also says, I recognize the city has difficult decisions to make. I'm not

04:12:01.073 --> 04:12:04.653
asking you to ignore public safety or the city's financial needs.

04:12:04.766 --> 04:12:08.009
I'm asking you to find a reasonable middle ground. So we'll get

04:12:08.041 --> 04:12:11.858
that part of the record. Another emailed, Carissa Ferris,

04:12:13.333 --> 04:12:16.090
also not here. She is new homeowner.

04:12:17.356 --> 04:12:21.027
Another lengthy comment, also opposing the

04:12:21.527 --> 04:12:25.899
tax increase. So we'll get that part of the record. We have Olivia Lund,

04:12:26.188 --> 04:12:29.554
who did fill out a paper but does not wish to make a verbal

04:12:30.054 --> 04:12:33.689
comment. I want to make sure that that was true for Olivia Lund. And her

04:12:34.189 --> 04:12:37.602
comment is, because you can't tax some of the most wealthy companies Our,

04:12:37.779 --> 04:12:41.587
our rent is being raised and we can't afford to ever buy now

04:12:42.358 --> 04:12:46.070
because we pay the difference for corporations. It's from Olivia.

04:12:47.178 --> 04:12:50.858
Uh, Mary Compton also wrote in but does

04:12:50.874 --> 04:12:54.506
not want to make a verbal comment, I believe. And she

04:12:55.006 --> 04:12:58.265
states, your job is to serve the people, present ideas to the people,

04:12:58.282 --> 04:13:02.299
and make decisions based on what the people need, not just a few people

04:13:02.799 --> 04:13:05.557
who want cleaner parks. Um, and she says,

04:13:06.857 --> 04:13:09.666
the rest of us are struggling to make the money stretch as well. You should

04:13:10.166 --> 04:13:13.293
also make the money stretch. And the last one we have for

04:13:13.793 --> 04:13:17.337
public comment is Emily Buss. She did send in a 2-page letter.

04:13:17.786 --> 04:13:19.712
I believe it did get to the mayor, but I don't think it got to

04:13:20.212 --> 04:13:23.516
council, so we'll make sure it gets to you as well. Um, she does say

04:13:23.564 --> 04:13:28.026
she believes there's a reasonable path forward, um, and does support

04:13:28.202 --> 04:13:32.102
the council considering a tax rate between 0.0009 and

04:13:32.602 --> 04:13:35.844
0.001. 0010547, and goes

04:13:36.344 --> 04:13:39.168
into some specifics, so I can make sure that that gets to you as well.

04:13:40.164 --> 04:13:44.002
The final comments that I do have have noted that it's for the public hearing

04:13:44.356 --> 04:13:47.552
on 13C on these last couple comments.

04:13:48.547 --> 04:13:50.941
That's all I have. Okay,

04:13:52.049 --> 04:13:55.341
the ones for 13C will still have a chance to speak. That— okay, I just

04:13:55.841 --> 04:13:58.730
want to make sure I heard that right. And, and, uh,

04:13:59.491 --> 04:14:03.175
We're nearing the end, so I just want to make sure, is there anyone else?

04:14:07.940 --> 04:14:09.004
Yeah, I'm waiting.

04:14:11.064 --> 04:14:15.132
So— I think we have Dale. He said he put in a paper,

04:14:15.148 --> 04:14:17.925
but I don't see it, so it might still be back there. But just go

04:14:18.425 --> 04:14:20.303
ahead and come up if you'd like, and you can fill the paper out after.

04:14:20.566 --> 04:14:23.745
Yeah, if that's okay. So state your name for the record, if you would.

04:14:27.870 --> 04:14:31.074
Hello, Dale Benson. Uh, thank you so much for,

04:14:31.911 --> 04:14:35.084
uh, having this discussion and,

04:14:35.148 --> 04:14:38.580
uh, being open. And thank you to the public too for coming out. I was

04:14:38.613 --> 04:14:41.467
kind of a latecomer to this conversation, but,

04:14:42.467 --> 04:14:45.272
uh, they, they did— some of my friends, they did, um,

04:14:47.396 --> 04:14:50.678
tell me I should come down. Um, I'm gonna have to side with

04:14:51.178 --> 04:14:53.845
the vast majority right now. against the tax increase.

04:14:54.664 --> 04:14:57.651
And I'll just, uh, give it a little context.

04:14:58.518 --> 04:15:01.874
I mean, I refer to the great Thomas Sowell,

04:15:02.291 --> 04:15:05.743
great economist, started out as a Marxist, thought the government should

04:15:06.243 --> 04:15:09.452
be doing all kinds of things. And then he learned, wow, this is the worst

04:15:09.517 --> 04:15:13.033
thing that's happening to my community. And he really

04:15:13.049 --> 04:15:16.437
started to understand. And, uh, I'm coming from California,

04:15:16.453 --> 04:15:19.647
so I've As I started learning more about politics and I

04:15:20.433 --> 04:15:23.915
started seeing how deceptive things were,

04:15:24.846 --> 04:15:28.488
we've seen this game so many— so often when it's taxes.

04:15:28.889 --> 04:15:31.489
Oh, it's going to be for— it's got to be for the fire department.

04:15:31.537 --> 04:15:34.168
It's got to be for the police. Oh, don't you want your kids to have

04:15:34.668 --> 04:15:39.544
education? It's always the same rodeo. And Thomas

04:15:40.044 --> 04:15:44.053
Sowell, I mean, the big picture, inflation is because government

04:15:44.553 --> 04:15:48.210
is spending. It's giving money and it's such malicious

04:15:48.710 --> 04:15:51.943
games that I saw in California. I mean, it gets to the point where they're

04:15:52.443 --> 04:15:56.461
buying votes. That's really what it's coming down to. What's the smallest

04:15:56.494 --> 04:16:00.407
common denominator that we can give people money to

04:16:00.439 --> 04:16:03.628
where they're going to vote for us and keep us in office? And now we're

04:16:04.128 --> 04:16:07.118
seeing tremendous fraud, and this borders on treasonous,

04:16:07.231 --> 04:16:11.695
what's happening. They're even bringing people that aren't Americans

04:16:11.840 --> 04:16:14.770
and Figuring out, hey, this is a great new voter class.

04:16:15.380 --> 04:16:18.941
There's all kinds of things that we're dealing with, but we're dealing with tremendous

04:16:19.069 --> 04:16:22.422
inflation. And I'm glad— I'm just going to side with

04:16:22.922 --> 04:16:26.945
everybody and say, you know what? The government gets to raise their

04:16:27.090 --> 04:16:30.426
wages and stuff. You get to open new city council buildings.

04:16:30.939 --> 04:16:33.201
You get to do all those things. Then, oh, we got a raise, but it's

04:16:33.345 --> 04:16:37.083
for the police. I mean, we've just seen this game so often,

04:16:37.676 --> 04:16:40.886
and of course, people working in the public sector. They might support it,

04:16:41.030 --> 04:16:43.198
whether you're in the schools or whether they're in the government.

04:16:44.322 --> 04:16:47.903
Hey, we need to raise— things are going up. But inflation,

04:16:49.139 --> 04:16:52.928
that every time they say we're going to give you money, now I'm

04:16:53.428 --> 04:16:56.942
realizing you're— we're going to lose so much in the future. You're going to pay

04:16:57.442 --> 04:17:00.491
for this. I mean, look what Biden was doing, giving money like crazy.

04:17:01.037 --> 04:17:03.847
And it's almost like, hey, I'm just practicing. So,

04:17:03.959 --> 04:17:07.458
Zelensky, Cloudward and Piven. Let's just

04:17:07.958 --> 04:17:12.736
destroy the whole system by overwhelming. I mean, there's a

